CHAPTERS = {'Hook': '做市商靠什么谋生？', 'Business': '1. 做市商的生意', 'Tape': '2. 在成交记录上做市', 'Fills': '3. 成交率与最优报价', 'Tick': '4. 跳价大小与队列位置', 'ETF': '5. 为交易所交易基金做市', 'Speed': '6. 速度竞赛', 'Industry': '7. 快速做市的经济学', 'House': '8. 第38条规则：只报你能测量的价', 'Research': '写给研究者：狙击均衡', 'Outro': '回顾、交易台问题与习题'}

ZH = {
    'Part thirty-eight. Market making, exchange-traded funds and the speed race: the business on the other side of every order in the last three parts, and why it has become a contest of microseconds.': '第38部分。做市、交易所交易基金与速度竞赛：前三部分里每一笔订单另一边的生意，以及它为什么变成了一场以微秒计的较量。',
    "A simple gross-spread story. <bookmark mark='a'/> Buy at the bid and sell at the offer, if both trades occur before value changes and other costs. <bookmark mark='b'/> In the selected Bitcoin perpetual snapshots a one-tick spread is common, about four hundredths of a basis point. <bookmark mark='c'/> What remains after marking the selected fills and inventory? This part compares model-based answers with a particular public-tape reconstruction.": "一个毛价差故事。<bookmark mark='a'/>在买价买入、卖价卖出，前提是两次都成交，且价值变化和其他成本尚未吞掉边际。<bookmark mark='b'/>指定比特币永续快照中，一档价差很常见，约0.04个基点。<bookmark mark='c'/>把选定成交与库存按中点标记后还剩什么？本部分比较模型答案与特定公开记录重建。",
    'f"Three results with different scopes. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> In our coarse-grid replay, the slow rule loses about {abs(d[\'slow\'][\'pnl_per_fill\']):.0f} ticks per fill marked to the final mid, and the rule that knows which trades will pass through it still loses {abs(d[\'fast\'][\'pnl_per_fill\']):.0f}. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Feeding reach proxies into a quoting model suggests roughly thirty ticks. A separate optimistic reach test has positive gross marks there, without queues, fees or an inventory strategy. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> A simplified sniping model has a spread independent of the number of equally fast firms. That is a conditional model result; ideal repricing in a batch removes its stale-quote prize."': "三个范围不同的结果。<bookmark mark='a'/>粗网格回放中，慢速规则按日终中点标记，每次成交约亏{abs(d['slow']['pnl_per_fill']):.0f}档；预先知道哪些成交会穿价的规则仍亏{abs(d['fast']['pnl_per_fill']):.0f}档。<bookmark mark='b'/>把触达代理输入报价模型，会得到约三十档的距离。另一项乐观触达实验在此处有正毛标记，但没有排队、费用或库存策略。<bookmark mark='c'/>简化狙击模型的价差与等速企业数量无关。这是条件模型结论；理想批量重定价按假设消除陈旧报价奖池。",
    "Why this matters. <bookmark mark='a'/> Electronic market makers are important liquidity suppliers across stocks, futures, currencies and crypto, alongside banks and other dealers. Shares vary by venue and product. <bookmark mark='b'/> They sell immediacy: an executable price now while they manage the position that results. <bookmark mark='c'/> Part thirty-seven's executor trades against them. ETF creation and redemption add a second route between share liquidity and the underlying basket.": "为什么要研究。<bookmark mark='a'/>电子做市商与银行等交易商共同为股票、期货、外汇和加密产品提供重要流动性，份额因市场而异。<bookmark mark='b'/>他们出售即时性：现在给出可执行价格，同时管理成交后形成的头寸。<bookmark mark='c'/>第37部分的执行者与他们交易。ETF申购赎回则在份额流动性与底层篮子之间再加一条通道。",
    "Three distinctions. <bookmark mark='a'/> Inventory need not express a directional investment thesis, although makers can use forecasts and may carry positions overnight. <bookmark mark='b'/> The spread is gross revenue. Our simple replay loses after marking its fills; this does not establish that professional makers have costs above revenue. <bookmark mark='c'/> Many firms manage portfolios of instruments and venues with hedges and capital constraints.": "三个区别。<bookmark mark='a'/>库存不一定代表方向性投资观点，但做市商可以使用预测，也可能隔夜持仓。<bookmark mark='b'/>价差是毛收入。简单回放在标记成交后亏损，并不能证明专业做市商成本高于收入。<bookmark mark='c'/>许多企业跨工具、跨场所管理组合，并考虑对冲与资本约束。",
    "Where this sits. Part thirty-five met the dealer in theory; Part thirty-six measured the queue, and Part thirty-seven the executor's cost. This part runs the dealer's business, closing Act six's look at microstructure before Part thirty-nine moves to crypto and decentralised finance.": '这一部分的位置。第35部分在理论中认识了交易商；第36部分测量了队列，第37部分测量了执行者的成本。这一部分经营交易商的生意，结束第六幕对微观结构的考察，之后第39部分转向加密货币与去中心化金融。',
    "Fifty years of the dealer's problem. Inventory models from Mark Garman, then Thomas Ho and Hans Stoll; Glosten and Milgrom's adverse selection; and in 1993 the first American ETF. <bookmark mark='a'/> Then Avellaneda and Stoikov's optimal quotes, the flash crash, Guéant, Lehalle and Fernandez-Tapia's closed form, and Albert Menkveld's study of a high-frequency market maker. <bookmark mark='b'/> And the speed race: batch auctions proposed, a speed bump approved, the economics of high-frequency trading, bond ETFs in March twenty twenty, and the race measured on the London Stock Exchange.": "交易商问题的五十年。加曼的库存模型，随后何与斯托尔，再有格洛斯滕和米尔格罗姆的逆向选择，以及1993年美国首只ETF。<bookmark mark='a'/>接着阿韦利亚内达与斯托伊科夫报价、闪崩、盖昂、勒阿勒与费尔南德斯塔皮亚闭式近似，以及门克韦尔德对一家高频做市商的研究。<bookmark mark='b'/>再到速度竞赛：批量拍卖建议、减速带获批、高频经济学、2020年3月债券ETF及伦敦逐消息竞赛研究。",
    'The plan: a consistent profit ledger; a coarse-grid maker replay; reach probabilities, model quotes and markout proxies; tick size and queues; ETF arbitrage and the historical policy chronology; the speed race and its economics; and a conditional sniping equilibrium, with a separate speed-investment game.': '本部分安排：一致的损益账本；粗网格做市回放；触达概率、模型报价与标记代理；最小价位和队列；ETF套利与政策历史时间线；速度竞赛及其经济学；最后是条件狙击角色均衡，以及另行规定的速度投资博弈。',
    'In the House, the market-making desk opens beside the execution desk: one sells immediacy, the other buys it, and each must know what the other is paying.': '在本系列公司里，做市台在执行台旁边开张：一个出售即时性，一个购买即时性，每一方都必须知道另一方在付多少钱。',
    'Chapter one. A market maker posts prices at which it will buy and sell, and lets others choose. Its profit is what remains after everyone who chose to trade with it has been paid for knowing more, or for being faster.': '第1章。做市商挂出愿意买入和卖出的价格，让别人来选择。它的利润，是付给每一个因为知道得更多或者更快而选择与它交易的人之后剩下的部分。',
    "The accounting first. <bookmark mark='a'/> Marked wealth is execution edge at each fill, plus rebates, plus gains on inventory as the mid moves. Epsilon is the taker's sign; the maker holds the opposite trade. This self-financing identity omits other costs. <bookmark mark='b'/> Separately, adverse markout is the subsequent mid move in the taker's direction at a specified horizon. <bookmark mark='c'/> Subtract that from the fill's execution edge to obtain a horizon-marked edge. This already includes that price move. Subtracting it again from the full inventory ledger would double-count it.": "先核算。<bookmark mark='a'/>标记财富等于每次成交的执行边际，加返佣，再加库存随中点变动的收益。艾普西隆代表主动方方向，做市商承担相反交易；这条自融资恒等式未计其他成本。<bookmark mark='b'/>另一个量是不利标记：指定时限内，中点沿主动方方向的后续变化。<bookmark mark='c'/>从入场执行边际中减它，得到时限标记边际，已经包含该价格变动。若再从完整库存账本扣一次，就重复计算了。",
    "Three risks. <bookmark mark='a'/> Adverse selection: the taker knows something, either private information or just a faster read of public news. <bookmark mark='b'/> Inventory: every fill leaves a position whose price risk the maker carries until the other side arrives. <bookmark mark='c'/> And operations: a quoting engine that misbehaves for minutes can lose more than a year of spreads. Knight Capital, as reported, lost about four hundred and forty million dollars in under an hour in August twenty twelve.": "三种风险。<bookmark mark='a'/>逆向选择：吃单者知道些什么，要么是私人信息，要么只是对公开消息读得更快。<bookmark mark='b'/>存货：每笔成交都留下一个仓位，在另一边到来之前，做市商承担它的价格风险。<bookmark mark='c'/>还有运营：一个出故障几分钟的报价引擎，可能亏掉超过一年的价差收入。据报道，Knight Capital在2012年8月不到一小时内亏损约4.4亿美元。",
    "A model-based spread decomposition. <bookmark mark='a'/> Stoll, then Huang and Stoll, distinguish order processing, inventory and adverse selection under their respective identification assumptions. <bookmark mark='b'/> Processing includes fees, technology and capital. <bookmark mark='c'/> Inventory carries price risk until it is offset. <bookmark mark='d'/> Adverse selection concerns conditional losses to counterparties. A simple replay's loss does not separately identify those structural components.": "模型下的价差分解。<bookmark mark='a'/>斯托尔及后来的黄与斯托尔，在各自识别假设下区分订单处理、库存和逆向选择。<bookmark mark='b'/>处理成本包含费用、技术和资本。<bookmark mark='c'/>库存承担抵消前的价格风险。<bookmark mark='d'/>逆向选择关注对手方相关的条件损失。简单回放的亏损不能分别识别这些结构成分。",
    "Recall the symmetric Glosten and Milgrom example. <bookmark mark='a'/> Value is high or low with equal prior probabilities. A fraction mu knows value; uninformed traders buy and sell with equal odds, independently of value. <bookmark mark='b'/> Conditional on a buy, high value has probability one plus mu over two. A risk-neutral competitive dealer therefore asks the conditional expected value. <bookmark mark='c'/> Spread is mu times the value range, with no fees or inventory risk. <bookmark mark='d'/> A fifth informed and a range of ten give two. <bookmark mark='e'/> Against eventual value, the expected adverse move equals the half-spread. This theoretical balance does not identify which real Bitcoin maker breaks even.": "回顾对称的格洛斯滕与米尔格罗姆例子。<bookmark mark='a'/>价值高低先验各半，比例缪的交易者知道价值；无信息者的买卖各半且独立于价值。<bookmark mark='b'/>给定买入，高价值概率为一加缪再除以二。风险中性竞争交易商按该条件期望报价。<bookmark mark='c'/>无费用、无库存风险时，价差是缪乘价值区间。<bookmark mark='d'/>五分之一知情、区间十，价差为二。<bookmark mark='e'/>相对最终价值，平均不利移动等于半价差。这一理论平衡不能识别现实中哪家比特币做市商恰好保本。",
    "The familiar Avellaneda and Stoikov approximation. <bookmark mark='a'/> Take a driftless Brownian mid, constant-size trades and CARA utility. The reservation-price approximation falls with inventory times remaining price variance. <bookmark mark='b'/> Its approximate total spread combines risk and an arrival-rate term. <bookmark mark='c'/> The model assumes exponential conditional arrival rates with price noise independent of the arrival drivers. A tape reach fit alone does not test those assumptions, queue fills or the control problem.": "常见的阿韦利亚内达与斯托伊科夫近似。<bookmark mark='a'/>假设无漂移布朗中点、固定单位成交与恒定绝对风险厌恶效用，保留价近似随库存乘剩余价格方差而下降。<bookmark mark='b'/>总价差近似包含风险项和到达率项。<bookmark mark='c'/>模型规定指数条件到达率，价格噪声与到达驱动独立。仅拟合记录触达，不能检验这些假设、队列成交或控制问题。",
    "A restricted revenue calculation. <bookmark mark='a'/> Suppose an independently arriving unit fill earns delta and has rate A times exp minus k delta. Ignore adverse selection, fees and inventory. <bookmark mark='b'/> Differentiating delta times that rate gives delta equals one over k as the unique interior maximum for positive A and k. <bookmark mark='c'/> Risk aversion can widen even zero-inventory quotes as well as skew them. This baseline is not a universal optimal trading distance.": "一个受限收入算例。<bookmark mark='a'/>假设独立到来的单位成交赚取德尔塔，速率为A乘指数负k德尔塔；忽略逆向选择、费用和库存。<bookmark mark='b'/>对距离乘速率求导，正A和k下唯一内点最大值为一除以k。<bookmark mark='c'/>风险厌恶既会加宽零库存报价，也会倾斜库存报价。这一基准不是普适最优交易距离。",
    'f"In numbers. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> An illustrative maker: risk aversion a tenth, variance still to bear of four, and a fill decay of one and a half. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The total spread is {total:.2f}, mostly the fill-rate term, close to two over k; the risk term adds only 0.4. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Holding two units, it centres its quotes 0.8 below the mid, to sell more and buy less."': "用数字来看。<bookmark mark='a'/>一个示例做市商：风险厌恶十分之一，仍需承担的方差为4，成交衰减为1.5。<bookmark mark='b'/>总价差是{total:.2f}，大部分是成交率项，接近k分之二；风险项只加了0.4。<bookmark mark='c'/>持有两个单位时，它把报价中心放在中间价下方0.8，以便多卖少买。",
    "The GLFT closed-form approximation. <bookmark mark='a'/> With positive A, k, gamma, a Brownian reference price, unit trades and bounded inventory, a long-horizon spectral problem gives stationary quotes. Away from binding boundaries, a further Gaussian approximation gives these formulas. <bookmark mark='b'/> A long maker raises its bid distance and lowers its ask distance. <bookmark mark='c'/> Sigma is price per square root of time. Calibration to reach proxies does not validate the arrival model; the finite-inventory exact limit also differs from this interior approximation.": "GLFT闭式近似。<bookmark mark='a'/>在正A、k、伽马，布朗参考价、单位成交和有界库存条件下，长时限谱问题给稳态报价。远离起作用的边界，再作高斯近似才得到这些公式。<bookmark mark='b'/>持多使买入距离增加、卖出距离减少。<bookmark mark='c'/>西格玛的单位为价格除以根号时间。用触达代理校准不验证到达模型；有限库存的精确极限也不同于这个内点近似。",
    "How the business changed. <bookmark mark='a'/> The New York Stock Exchange historically assigned specialists with quoting obligations and privileged book information. <bookmark mark='b'/> Christie and Schultz documented avoidance of odd eighths on Nasdaq in 1994; investigations and settlements followed. <bookmark mark='c'/> Decimalization and electronic competition changed those institutions and narrowed many spreads. Specialist functions evolved rather than disappearing everywhere at once.": "行业怎样变化。<bookmark mark='a'/>纽约证交所历史上分配专营商，附带报价义务与特有订单簿信息。<bookmark mark='b'/>克里斯蒂和舒尔茨在1994年记录纳斯达克回避奇数八分之一报价，随后有调查及和解。<bookmark mark='c'/>十进制化与电子竞争改变这些制度并缩小许多价差，专营功能经历演变，而非所有市场同时消失。",
    "Who does it today. <bookmark mark='a'/> In American stocks, wholesalers internalise most retail orders off exchange and pay brokers for the flow. <bookmark mark='b'/> Electronic market makers quote on exchanges in thousands of instruments at once; Virtu disclosed a single losing day in about twelve hundred, as Part thirty-four discussed. <bookmark mark='c'/> And some venues contract designated makers to quote within a maximum spread for a minimum share of the day, in return for rebates or priority.": "今天由谁来做。<bookmark mark='a'/>在美国股票市场，批发商在交易所之外内部化大部分零售订单，并为订单流向券商付费。<bookmark mark='b'/>电子做市商同时在交易所为数千种工具报价；正如第34部分所讨论的，Virtu披露在约一千二百个交易日中只有一天亏损。<bookmark mark='c'/>有些交易场所与指定做市商签约，要求他们在一天中的最低比例时间内、以不超过某个上限的价差报价，作为交换获得返佣或优先权。",
    "Order flow differs. <bookmark mark='a'/> Retail flow often has lower average adverse markout than professional arbitrage flow, but neither label proves that an individual order is informed. <bookmark mark='b'/> Segmentation can change the flow remaining on exchanges; its effect on lit spreads depends on competition and routing, rather than following mechanically from payment for order flow. <bookmark mark='c'/> Makers measure markouts by size, time and available counterparty classifications to estimate those differences.": "订单流不同。<bookmark mark='a'/>零售流平均不利标记往往小于专业套利流，但任何标签都不能证明某一订单知情。<bookmark mark='b'/>流量分层会改变留在交易所的订单，其对公开价差的影响依赖竞争和路由，不能由订单流付款机械推出。<bookmark mark='c'/>做市商按数量、时间及可得对手方分类测量标记，估计这些差异。",
    "Real makers run many books at once. <bookmark mark='a'/> A maker in a thousand stocks hedges the common factor with index futures and keeps the stock-specific inventory small: Part thirty-one's risk model, at high frequency. <bookmark mark='b'/> An options maker quotes a whole volatility surface and hedges its Greeks, as in Part eleven. <bookmark mark='c'/> And in crypto the same Bitcoin trades on many venues, as spot and perpetual: makers quote on several and hedge on the cheapest.": "真正的做市商同时经营许多账本。<bookmark mark='a'/>一家为一千只股票做市的公司用股指期货对冲共同因子，把个股存货保持得很小：高频版的第31部分风险模型。<bookmark mark='b'/>期权做市商为整个波动率曲面报价，并对冲它的希腊字母，就像第11部分那样。<bookmark mark='c'/>在加密市场，同一个比特币在许多交易场所以现货和永续合约的形式交易：做市商在几个场所报价，在最便宜的地方对冲。",
    'Pause and predict. In the specified coarse-grid maker replay, orders join behind displayed quantity, with assumed pro-rata cancellations and through-price fills. After execution price is marked to the mid one minute later, would a half-tick quoted spread alone imply positive mean profit? Predict the sign before viewing the measured conditional mark.': '暂停预测。指定粗网格回放中，订单排在显示量之后，按假设比例分配撤单，穿价成交视作执行。成交价在一分钟后按中点标记，只有半档报价价差就能推出正平均利润吗？先预测符号，再看测得的条件标记。',
    'f"Chapter two, answering the pause. The slow rule has a one-minute signed mark of {d[\'mk60\']:.1f} ticks per fill. Its separate final-mid profit mean is {d[\'pnl_per_fill\']:.1f}. Both omit fees and executable liquidation. We will keep the horizon and fill-selection rules visible."': "第2章，回答暂停。慢速规则的一分钟有符号标记为每次成交{d['mk60']:.1f}档，另一个日终中点利润均值为{d['pnl_per_fill']:.1f}档。两者都未计费用与可执行平仓。我们始终注明时限及成交筛选规则。",
    "The simulated maker. <bookmark mark='a'/> It posts one unit behind displayed quantity while assuming its own orders do not change prices. <bookmark mark='b'/> It reconstructs events on a hundred-millisecond grid, canceling or retaining old levels under the source's priority rules. <bookmark mark='c'/> Inventory is limited to five units each way. <bookmark mark='d'/> At-price volume must exceed the queue ahead; cancellations are allocated pro rata and trades through the price fill. These are reconstruction assumptions, not message-level queue observations.": "模拟做市商。<bookmark mark='a'/>在显示量之后报一单位，同时假设自己的订单不改变价格。<bookmark mark='b'/>以100毫秒网格重建事件，按照源码的优先规则撤单或保留旧价位。<bookmark mark='c'/>双向库存上限五单位。<bookmark mark='d'/>同价成交量必须超过前方数量；撤单按比例分配，穿价成交执行。这些是重建假设，不是逐消息队列观测。",
    'f"On the seventeenth of May. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The slow rule has {s[\'n\']:,} fills, roughly half a tick of pre-step execution edge, an average same-step mid move of {s[\'step\']:.1f}, and final-mid profit of {s[\'pnl_per_fill\']:.1f} ticks per fill. The separate one-minute column is {s[\'mk60\']:.1f}. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The fast variant knows all trades in the step before deciding whether a through-price fill survives, and has final-mid profit {f[\'pnl_per_fill\']:.1f}. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Adding the imbalance rule gives {ff[\'pnl_per_fill\']:.1f}. The variants select different fills and inventory paths, so this is not an identified causal speed effect."': "5月17日。<bookmark mark='a'/>慢速规则有{s['n']:,}次成交，步前执行边际约半档，同一步中点平均变动{s['step']:.1f}档，日终利润每次{s['pnl_per_fill']:.1f}档。另一个一分钟列为{s['mk60']:.1f}档。<bookmark mark='b'/>快速变体先知道该步全部交易，再决定穿价成交是否保留，日终利润为{f['pnl_per_fill']:.1f}档。<bookmark mark='c'/>加上失衡规则为{ff['pnl_per_fill']:.1f}档。各变体选择不同成交和库存路径，因此不是识别出的因果速度效果。",
    "A decomposition of the slow rule's signed one-minute mark. <bookmark mark='a'/> Pre-step execution edge, then the same-step mid move, then increments to the one-second, ten-second and one-minute marks. Those components telescope to the one-minute statistic; the half-spread is already included. <bookmark mark='b'/> The same-step increment is the largest single negative piece here, but later movement matters too. A grid cannot recover exact ordering or an actual cancel latency within that step.": "分解慢速规则的一分钟有符号标记。<bookmark mark='a'/>先有步前执行边际，再加同一步中点变动，以及到一秒、十秒、一分钟的增量。这些项望远镜相消后等于一分钟统计，半价差已包含在内。<bookmark mark='b'/>同一步增量是此处最大的单项负值，但之后的变化也重要。网格不能恢复该步内的精确顺序或实际撤单延迟。",
    "Signed marks for three different selected fill sets. <bookmark mark='a'/> The first point uses the previous grid mid, the next includes the fill step, followed by one, ten and sixty grid-second marks. Near the day end, horizons are clipped. <bookmark mark='b'/> All three minute means are negative, with the filtered set least negative. This documents conditional marks under the reconstruction. It does not separate causal speed, predictive skill or market impact.": "三个不同筛选成交集合的有符号标记。<bookmark mark='a'/>第一点用前一网格中点，下一点纳入成交所在步，再看一秒、十秒、六十秒网格时限；接近日末时会截断。<bookmark mark='b'/>三组一分钟均值都负，过滤组最少负。这记录的是重建条件下的标记，并不能分离因果速度、预测能力或市场冲击。",
    "What the imbalance filter changes. <bookmark mark='a'/> It removes nearly two-thirds of the hindsight variant's selected fills. <bookmark mark='b'/> The retained set has a less negative one-second signed mark. <bookmark mark='c'/> The final-mid total loss also falls, with both a lower count and a changed mean. A product decomposition depends on the chosen reference mean; these selected comparisons do not by themselves identify a causal forecast benefit.": "失衡过滤改变什么。<bookmark mark='a'/>它删除事后快速变体近三分之二的选定成交。<bookmark mark='b'/>留下的集合一秒有符号标记较少负。<bookmark mark='c'/>日终总损失也下降，笔数和均值同时改变。乘积分解依赖选定参照均值；这些筛选比较本身不识别因果预测收益。",
    "Possible mechanisms, not identified counterparties. <bookmark mark='a'/> Cross-venue information can make a quote stale. <bookmark mark='b'/> Liquidations can generate one-sided aggressive flow. <bookmark mark='c'/> Other makers may withdraw ahead of a move. Our single-venue aggregate tape does not identify these trader types or attribute each replay loss to them.": "可能机制，而非已识别的对手方。<bookmark mark='a'/>跨场所信息可能使报价陈旧。<bookmark mark='b'/>强平可能产生单向主动流。<bookmark mark='c'/>其他做市商可能在变动前撤回。单场所归集记录不能识别这些交易者身份，也不能把每项回放损失归因于它们。",
    'f"Compare the replay variants. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The slow rule accepts through-price fills. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The idealized fast rule discards them with within-step hindsight. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Their final-mid means differ by about {gap:.0f} ticks per selected fill. Different denominators and inventory paths prevent interpreting this as the causal value of a latency improvement or a universal upper bound."': "比较回放变体。<bookmark mark='a'/>慢速规则接受穿价成交。<bookmark mark='b'/>理想快速规则利用步内事后信息删除它们。<bookmark mark='c'/>各自选定成交的日终均值相差约{gap:.0f}档。分母与库存路径不同，不能解释为延迟改善的因果价值或普适速度上界。",
    'f"The inventory statistic. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> A hard five-unit limit is the rule\'s only explicit inventory control. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Inventory standard deviation is {d[\'slow\'][\'inv_sd\']:.1f} units over the grid path. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> At a boundary it stops posting one side. Standard deviation does not report boundary occupancy or prove what causes it. GLFT supplies an alternative control model, whose performance this replay has not evaluated."': "库存统计。<bookmark mark='a'/>五单位硬上限是规则唯一明确的库存控制。<bookmark mark='b'/>网格路径上的库存标准差为{d['slow']['inv_sd']:.1f}单位。<bookmark mark='c'/>到边界时停止一侧报价；标准差不报告边界占用，也不证明原因。GLFT是另一控制模型，本回放未评估它的表现。",
    'f"On three days, two weekdays and a Saturday. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The ordering never changes: slow worst, fast better, fast and filtered best, but never positive; the best day is {best:.1f} ticks a fill. A quoting rule with no forecast of its own, at the touch, on this market, pays its counterparties."': "在三天里，两个工作日和一个星期六。<bookmark mark='a'/>排序从未改变：慢的最差，快的较好，快而过滤的最好，但从不为正；最好的一天是每笔{best:.1f}跳。一个没有自身预测、在最优价位、在这个市场上的报价规则，是在给它的对手方付钱。",
    'f"Converting the illustrative final-mid loss. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> One ten-cent tick is {tb:.3f} basis points at the day\'s representative price. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The filtered rule\'s mean loss is {need:.2f} basis points per fill under this conversion. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> A constant rebate of that size would offset this chosen gross replay loss arithmetically. It is not a complete break-even estimate: hedging, liquidation, funding, latency and market impact are absent."': "换算指定的日终标记损失。<bookmark mark='a'/>按当日代表价，0.10美元一档等于{tb:.3f}基点。<bookmark mark='b'/>过滤规则平均亏损换算为每次成交{need:.2f}基点。<bookmark mark='c'/>同样大小的固定返佣可在算术上抵消该毛回放损失，但不是完整保本估计：缺少对冲、平仓、资金费、延迟和市场冲击。",
    "What remains unmeasured. <bookmark mark='a'/> The fast rule uses within-step hindsight; the data cannot certify real cancel speed or order precedence inside one hundred milliseconds. <bookmark mark='b'/> Queue position is reconstructed. Part thirty-six's front and back results compare different selected fill sets and are not causal priority prices. <bookmark mark='c'/> Cross-venue hedging, fees, funding and executable inventory liquidation are missing. The conclusion is limited to these specified replay rules.": "尚未测量的内容。<bookmark mark='a'/>快速规则有步内事后信息，数据不能认证实际撤单速度或100毫秒内的订单先后。<bookmark mark='b'/>队列位置是重建的。第36部分前后位置结果比较不同选定成交集，不是因果优先价格。<bookmark mark='c'/>缺少跨场所对冲、费用、资金费和可执行库存平仓。结论仅限这些规定回放规则。",
    "Pause and predict. Avellaneda and Stoikov's model assumes quotes fill at a rate that decays exponentially with their distance from the mid. Fitted to Bitcoin's tape, how far away would its optimal quotes sit: one tick, five, or thirty?": '暂停并预测。Avellaneda和Stoikov的模型假设报价的成交速率随它离中间价的距离指数衰减。用比特币的成交记录拟合，它的最优报价会离中间价多远：一跳、五跳，还是三十跳？',
    "f'Chapter three. At the lowest chosen risk aversion, the GLFT approximation gives {half:.0f} ticks from the mid. Its inputs include a reach-probability proxy rather than observed resting fills. We will compare it with a separate gross mark calculation, without claiming an optimized or profitable live strategy.'": '第3章。选定最低风险厌恶时，GLFT近似给距中点{half:.0f}档。输入包含触达概率代理，而非观测到的排队订单成交。我们与另一毛标记计算比较，不声称优化或盈利的实盘策略。',
    "Measure reach first. <bookmark mark='a'/> At each second's start, take the mid from the hundred-millisecond quote grid. <bookmark mark='b'/> Count separately whether buy trades reach an ask-distance threshold and sell trades reach a bid-distance threshold, then average the two probabilities. <bookmark mark='c'/> Minus log one minus probability divided by one second is the equivalent rate for a homogeneous Poisson event. This transformation does not establish Poisson arrivals or queue fills. <bookmark mark='d'/> Fit log rate against distance: its slope is minus k. The pooled fit averages daily probabilities before taking the logarithm, not daily intensities.": "先测触达。<bookmark mark='a'/>每秒开始，取100毫秒报价网格中点。<bookmark mark='b'/>分别统计主动买单是否达到卖侧距离、主动卖单是否达到买侧距离，再平均两概率。<bookmark mark='c'/>负对数一减概率除以一秒，是具有同样无事件概率的齐次泊松等效速率，不证明泊松到达或队列成交。<bookmark mark='d'/>拟合对数速率与距离，斜率是负k。汇总拟合先平均每日概率再取对数，不是平均每日强度。",
    'f"The two-day reach fit. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> A half-tick threshold is reached on about a third of the averaged side-windows; a forty-five-tick threshold on about one in twenty. These are side reach events, not actual fill counts. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The fitted k is {f[\'k\']:.3f} per tick, so the equivalent rate halves over about {half_d:.0f} ticks. The near point lies above the fitted line. Large threshold reaches can accompany trading and price moves; the grid does not identify a message-level sweep mechanism."': "两天触达拟合。<bookmark mark='a'/>半档阈值在平均每侧窗口约三分之一被达到，四十五档约二十分之一。这是侧向触达事件，不是实际成交数。<bookmark mark='b'/>拟合k为{f['k']:.3f}/档，等效速率每约{half_d:.0f}档减半。近点高于拟合线。大阈值触达可伴随交易和价格变化，网格不能识别逐消息扫单机制。",
    'f"Across the two days, fitted k is {k0:.3f} and {k1:.3f}. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> These descriptive differences accompany different flow and volatility. They do not prove a sweep mechanism or parameter stability. Pooled probabilities are averaged with equal day weights before conversion to an equivalent rate. A live estimator would need a specified past-only window and out-of-sample validation."': "两天拟合k分别为{k0:.3f}与{k1:.3f}。<bookmark mark='a'/>描述性差异伴随不同流量和波动，不能证明扫单机制或参数稳定。汇总先等权平均每日概率，再换等效速率。实时估计需规定仅用过去的窗口，并作样本外验证。",
    'f"Compare the equivalent reach rates with the fitted exponential. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The half-tick rate is {touch:.0f} percent above the fit. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> From one through thirty ticks, the mean absolute relative deviation over these chosen points is {mid_err:.0f} percent. That is a descriptive in-sample residual, without a confidence interval. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> At forty-five ticks the deviation is {tail:.0f} percent. <bookmark mark=\'d\'/> Near and far thresholds need not share one constant exponential law. Neither the residual pattern nor a log-linear fit tests independent arrivals, actual queue fills or an optimal quoting policy."': "比较等效触达速率和拟合指数。<bookmark mark='a'/>半档速率高于拟合{touch:.0f}%。<bookmark mark='b'/>选定一至三十档各点的平均绝对相对偏差为{mid_err:.0f}%，这是无置信区间的样本内描述残差。<bookmark mark='c'/>四十五档偏差为{tail:.0f}%。<bookmark mark='d'/>近远阈值不一定共用一个恒定指数规律。残差或对数线性拟合都不能检验独立到达、实际队列成交或最优报价策略。",
    'f"Feed the proxies into the GLFT approximation. Sigma is the standard deviation of one-second mid increments, about {g[\'sigma\']:.0f} ticks per square root of a second, without a claim that the price is Brownian. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> At gamma equal to one ten-thousandth per tick-unit, half-spread is {r0[\'half_spread\']:.0f} ticks. At one hundredth it is {r2[\'half_spread\']:.0f}, with inventory skew {r2[\'skew\']:.0f} ticks per unit. Unit size, risk preference, arrival assumptions and interior approximation matter. This is a model output, not a verified optimal quote."': "把代理输入GLFT近似。西格玛是一秒中点增量标准差，约{g['sigma']:.0f}档/根号秒，不声称价格就是布朗运动。<bookmark mark='a'/>伽马为每档单位的万分之一时，半价差{r0['half_spread']:.0f}档；百分之一时为{r2['half_spread']:.0f}档，库存倾斜每单位{r2['skew']:.0f}档。单位数量、风险偏好、到达假设及内点近似都重要。这是模型输出，不是已验证的最优报价。",
    'f"A separate reach experiment. At each second\'s starting mid, set two distance thresholds. Count at most one reach per side per window, and mark it at the mid sixty seconds after the window started, not sixty seconds after an exact fill time. No queue, tick rounding, fees or endogenous inventory are modeled. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The gross mean at five ticks is {r5[\'pnl60\']:.0f} ticks. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> It is {r30[\'pnl60\']:+.0f} at thirty and {r45[\'pnl60\']:+.0f} at forty-five. Agreement in distance does not validate the control model or establish executable profit."': "另一项触达实验。每秒起始中点两侧各设阈值，每侧每窗最多计一次触达，以窗口开始后六十秒中点标记，而非准确成交后六十秒。没有排队、档位取整、费用或内生库存。<bookmark mark='a'/>五档处毛均值为{r5['pnl60']:.0f}档。<bookmark mark='b'/>三十档为{r30['pnl60']:+.0f}，四十五档为{r45['pnl60']:+.0f}。距离相近不验证控制模型，也不建立可执行利润。",
    'f"Aggregate the reach marks per elapsed hour, counting one hypothetical unit per reached side-window. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> At two ticks, the loss is about {abs(r2[\'per_hour60\']):,.0f} tick-units per hour. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> At thirty it is {r30[\'per_hour60\']:+,.0f}. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> At forty-five it is {r45[\'per_hour60\']:+,.0f}, about seven hundred dollars if a unit is one bitcoin. Windows overlap, final windows are excluded while full elapsed time is used, and inventories are unconstrained. These sums are gross marks, not returns on a specified capital base."': "按每个触达侧窗一假想单位，将毛标记按经过小时加总。<bookmark mark='a'/>两档处每小时约亏{abs(r2['per_hour60']):,.0f}档单位。<bookmark mark='b'/>三十档为{r30['per_hour60']:+,.0f}。<bookmark mark='c'/>四十五档为{r45['per_hour60']:+,.0f}；一单位若为一比特币，约七百美元。窗口重叠，末端窗口被排除但分母用全部时间，库存不受限。这是毛标记和，不是指定资本的收益率。",
    'f"Interpreting the positive far-distance marks. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> A threshold reached during a large trade can lie beyond the later mid, consistent with an overshoot story; the calculation does not identify its cause. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> At forty-five ticks there are about {r45[\'fills_per_hour\']:.0f} reached side-windows per hour. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Optimistic fill treatment is not a mathematical upper bound on every feasible strategy. Queue priority, tick feasibility, overlapping positions and subsequent liquidation are missing."': "解释远距离正标记。<bookmark mark='a'/>大成交触达的阈值可能超过后续中点，与过冲故事一致，但计算不识别原因。<bookmark mark='b'/>四十五档每小时约{r45['fills_per_hour']:.0f}个触达侧窗。<bookmark mark='c'/>乐观执行不等于所有可行策略的数学上界；缺少队列优先、合法价位、重叠仓位和后续平仓。",
    "What the comparison tests. <bookmark mark='a'/> In the baseline model, arrival drivers are independent of the Brownian price noise, while controls can adapt to the current state. <bookmark mark='b'/> Conditional tape marks reveal dependence that a constant-rate independent-driver model omits. Similarity of a suggested distance and a gross-mark crossing is not validation. <bookmark mark='c'/> State-dependent arrivals and adverse-selection models are possible extensions. Their forecasts must be validated at actual decision times, with fills and costs.": "比较检验什么。<bookmark mark='a'/>基准模型里，到达驱动独立于布朗价格噪声，但控制可适应当前状态。<bookmark mark='b'/>条件记录标记显示恒定速率独立驱动模型遗漏的依赖。建议距离与毛标记过零相似不是验证。<bookmark mark='c'/>状态依赖到达及逆向选择模型是可能扩展，预测必须在实际决策时点，用成交和成本验证。",
    "A schematic way to add a forecast. <bookmark mark='a'/> Shift a quote center by an expected price move with matching price units, while solving the chosen model's inventory and arrival problem. This is not the full Cartea, Jaimungal and Ricci solution. <bookmark mark='b'/> The horizon must match the quote decision and possible fill time. <bookmark mark='c'/> Part thirty-six supplies descriptive state-conditioned means as candidate features, not validated executable alpha or proof that one estimator is always preferable.": "示意怎样加预测。<bookmark mark='a'/>用量纲相同的预期价格变化移动报价中心，同时求解选定库存和到达问题。这不是卡特亚、贾伊蒙加尔与里奇的完整解。<bookmark mark='b'/>时限须匹配报价决策和可能成交时间。<bookmark mark='c'/>第36部分描述性的状态条件均值只是候选特征，不是验证过的可执行阿尔法，也不能证明某估计器总更优。",
    "Pause and predict. Bitcoin's perpetual sits at a one-tick spread almost all the time. If the tick were ten times smaller, would the spread shrink ten times? Who would gain, and who would lose?": '暂停并预测。比特币永续合约几乎一直停在一跳的价差。如果跳价缩小十倍，价差会缩小十倍吗？谁会得益，谁会受损？',
    'Chapter four, and the answer to the pause: no. On a book pinned at one tick, a smaller tick lets the spread narrow only to where competition would put it, and it moves the contest from queue position to price. Takers gain from the narrower spread; makers who held the front of long queues lose their rent.': '第4章，以及暂停问题的答案：不会。在钉在一跳的订单簿上，更小的跳价只让价差收窄到竞争会把它推到的地方，并把竞争从队列位置转到价格上。吃单者从更窄的价差中得益；占据长队列前端的做市商失去他们的租金。',
    "A pinned spread. <bookmark mark='a'/> When the spread makers would accept is smaller than the tick, <bookmark mark='b'/> the spread sits at one tick and the queues grow long: makers who would undercut each other cannot. <bookmark mark='c'/> So they compete for priority instead of price, and priority goes to whoever arrives first: a race in speed.": "被钉住的价差。<bookmark mark='a'/>当做市商愿意接受的价差小于一跳时，<bookmark mark='b'/>价差停在一跳，队列变长：本来会互相压价的做市商无法压价。<bookmark mark='c'/>于是他们争夺优先权而不是价格，而优先权属于先到的人：一场速度竞赛。",
    'f"A rough model substitution. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Treat the aggregate trade count, about {bt[\'lam_i\']:.0f} per second, as a proxy investor rate. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Net mid changes of at least five ticks occur about {bt[\'lam_j\']:.2f} per second, with mean size {bt[\'J\']:.0f}. These are not identified public-news events or unit uninformed arrivals. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The formula then gives {bt[\'half\']:.2f} tick. <bookmark mark=\'d\'/> That is below the quoted half-tick floor in this illustrative model. It does not establish the actual natural spread, rent, or the source of the replay losses."': "粗略代入模型。<bookmark mark='a'/>把归集成交数约每秒{bt['lam_i']:.0f}次当投资者速率代理。<bookmark mark='b'/>至少五档净中点变化约每秒{bt['lam_j']:.2f}次，平均{bt['J']:.0f}档；它们不是识别出的公共新闻或无信息单位到达。<bookmark mark='c'/>公式给{bt['half']:.2f}档。<bookmark mark='d'/>该说明模型中低于报价半档下限，不能建立真实自然价差、租金或回放亏损来源。",
    "Queue priority changes who can execute. <bookmark mark='a'/> Part thirty-six compared front and back replay functionals on different filled sets. Their gap was not a causal price for moving one order forward. <bookmark mark='b'/> Posting earlier can obtain priority, subject to cancellation and queue rules. <bookmark mark='c'/> Some futures use pro-rata size allocation or hybrid rules. Those designs change incentives, but their welfare cannot be inferred from one replay.": "优先位置改变谁能成交。<bookmark mark='a'/>第36部分比较前后位置的毛回放函数，成交集合不同，差距不是把同一订单前移的因果价格。<bookmark mark='b'/>较早挂单可取得优先，但取决于撤单和队列规则。<bookmark mark='c'/>某些期货按量或混合分配，这改变激励，其福利不能由单个回放推出。",
    "Another way to share a pinned spread. <bookmark mark='a'/> Time priority, the rule of most stock and crypto books, makes speed buy position. <bookmark mark='b'/> Pro-rata matching, used in some interest-rate futures, splits each incoming order across the resting orders in proportion to their size. <bookmark mark='c'/> Then makers post far more than they want, because fills scale with size: the race moves from speed to size, and displayed depth overstates what anyone intends to trade.": "分享被钉住的价差的另一种方式。<bookmark mark='a'/>时间优先，大多数股票和加密订单簿的规则，让速度买到位置。<bookmark mark='b'/>按比例撮合，用于某些利率期货，把每笔进来的订单按挂单数量的比例分给各个挂单。<bookmark mark='c'/>于是做市商挂出远多于自己想要的数量，因为成交随数量增长：竞赛从速度转向数量，显示的深度夸大了人们真正想交易的量。",
    "Recall the chosen queue reconstruction. <bookmark mark='a'/> Its back-of-queue filled orders have a median wait around three seconds, with roughly four in five submissions filled within a minute. <bookmark mark='b'/> Front placement has a median around a fifth of a second. <bookmark mark='c'/> These conditional waiting summaries and fill probabilities have different censoring and selected sets. Smaller adverse marks do not identify less informed trader identities or a causal gain from priority.": "回顾指定队列重建。<bookmark mark='a'/>后排已成交订单的中位等待约三秒，约五分之四提交在一分钟内成交。<bookmark mark='b'/>前排中位数约五分之一秒。<bookmark mark='c'/>条件等待摘要和成交概率有不同删失与筛选集合。较少不利标记不能识别对手方更少知情，也不能识别优先带来的因果收益。",
    "So what is the right tick? <bookmark mark='a'/> Too large, and spreads are set by the rule, queues are long, and makers spend on speed. <bookmark mark='b'/> Too small, and anyone can step ahead of a queue by a trivial amount, so quotes flicker and the best levels thin out. <bookmark mark='c'/> Khalil Dayri and Mathieu Rosenbaum proposed choosing the tick so the average spread sits a little above one tick, where competition on price works and quotes are still worth posting.": "那么合适的跳价是多少？<bookmark mark='a'/>太大，价差由规则决定，队列很长，做市商在速度上花钱。<bookmark mark='b'/>太小，任何人都能以微不足道的金额插到队列前面，报价闪烁，最优档位变薄。<bookmark mark='c'/>Khalil Dayri和Mathieu Rosenbaum建议选择跳价，使平均价差略高于一跳，在那里价格竞争起作用，挂单也仍然值得。",
    "A static fee illustration with a common price benchmark. <bookmark mark='a'/> Hold the mid fixed, with one tick between bid and ask. <bookmark mark='b'/> A taker round trip pays that spread plus two equal per-unit taker fees. <bookmark mark='c'/> A maker completing the opposite round trip earns it plus two equal rebates, before adverse marks and other costs. Fees must use matching price units; changing prices and inventory prevent interpreting this as unconditional profit.": "用共同价格基准作静态费用说明。<bookmark mark='a'/>中点固定，买卖相隔一档。<bookmark mark='b'/>主动方往返付一档加两次相同单位费用。<bookmark mark='c'/>做市方完成相反往返赚一档加两次相同返佣，尚未计不利标记和其他成本。费用量纲须匹配价格；价格变化和库存使它不能作为无条件利润。",
    "So who gains when the tick shrinks? <bookmark mark='a'/> Once it no longer binds, competition sets the spread. <bookmark mark='b'/> Takers pay less per trade. <bookmark mark='c'/> The makers who won the queue race lose their rent. And the displayed depth at the best thins out, which can make large orders costlier even as small ones get cheaper.": "那么跳价缩小时谁得益？<bookmark mark='a'/>一旦它不再约束，竞争决定价差。<bookmark mark='b'/>吃单者每笔交易付得更少。<bookmark mark='c'/>赢得队列竞赛的做市商失去他们的租金。最优档位显示的深度也会变薄，这可能让大订单更贵，即使小订单变便宜。",
    "Historical rule changes. <bookmark mark='a'/> The United States tick-size pilot ran from twenty sixteen to twenty eighteen for selected small stocks. Published evaluations found wider spreads and changed displayed depth, with mixed investor effects. <bookmark mark='b'/> The SEC adopted half-cent increments for qualifying stocks in twenty twenty-four. Adoption and compliance are separate dates; this is a historical example, not a statement of the rule currently in force. <bookmark mark='c'/> Crypto venues also revise increments, changing queue and price incentives.": "历史规则变化。<bookmark mark='a'/>美国最小价位试点在2016至2018年覆盖选定小盘股，研究发现更宽价差和显示深度变化，投资者效果不一。<bookmark mark='b'/>证监会在2024年通过合资格股票半美分价位，采纳与执行日不同；这里是历史例子，不声称规则目前已经生效。<bookmark mark='c'/>加密场所也会修改价位，改变队列和价格激励。",
    'Pause and predict. An ETF holding corporate bonds trades at eighty dollars, while the published value of its bonds is eighty-four. Who could profit, how, and why might they not?': '暂停并预测。一只持有公司债的ETF价格为八十美元，而它所持债券的公布价值是八十四美元。谁可能获利，怎么做，又为什么可能做不到？',
    'Chapter five, and the answer to the pause: an authorised participant could buy the cheap ETF, redeem it for the bonds, and sell the bonds, if the bonds could really be sold at their published value. In March twenty twenty, often they could not. Exchange-traded funds are market making with a second exit.': '第5章，以及暂停问题的答案：授权参与者可以买入便宜的ETF，赎回换成债券，再卖出债券，前提是债券真的能按公布价值卖出去。在2020年3月，往往卖不出去。交易所交易基金是有第二个出口的做市。',
    "Creation and redemption mechanics. <bookmark mark='a'/> In an in-kind structure, an authorized participant delivers a specified basket for creation-unit shares. <bookmark mark='b'/> Redemption reverses that exchange, subject to the fund's terms; cash structures differ. <bookmark mark='c'/> NAV per share is marked assets minus liabilities, divided by shares outstanding. It is not necessarily an executable basket price. <bookmark mark='d'/> Secondary-market share trades between investors and market makers do not each trigger a primary transaction with the fund.": "申购赎回机制。<bookmark mark='a'/>实物结构中，授权参与者按指定篮子换创建单位份额。<bookmark mark='b'/>赎回按基金条款反向交换，现金结构不同。<bookmark mark='c'/>每份净值为资产标记减负债再除以份额，不一定是可执行篮子价。<bookmark mark='d'/>投资者与做市商的二级交易并非每一笔都触发与基金的一级申赎。",
    "A conditional arbitrage band. <bookmark mark='a'/> If the ETF sale proceeds exceed the executable basket purchase cost plus creation, financing and settlement costs, a participant can create and sell. <bookmark mark='b'/> Reverse the transactions for redemption at a discount. <bookmark mark='c'/> The displayed NAV inequalities are a shorthand only when NAV approximates the executable basket. Stale marks, hedging error, trading restrictions and capital constraints prevent a hard bound around published NAV.": "有条件的套利区间。<bookmark mark='a'/>若份额卖款超过可执行篮子买价加申购、融资和结算成本，参与者可以申购后卖出。<bookmark mark='b'/>折价赎回时反向交易。<bookmark mark='c'/>屏幕净值不等式只在净值近似可执行篮子时才是简写。陈旧标记、对冲误差、交易限制和资本约束，阻止围绕公布净值的硬界。",
    'f"A chosen executable-basket calculation. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Buy a share for eighty dollars. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Assume the delivered basket really sells for eighty-four gross, with a two-percent selling cost applied to that gross amount. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Net proceeds are eighty-two dollars thirty-two, a profit of {gain:.2f} before other costs. <bookmark mark=\'d\'/> If executable gross is only seventy-nine despite the published mark, the same cost leaves seventy-seven dollars forty-two, a loss of two dollars fifty-eight. The example illustrates why a marked NAV need not be an executable arbitrage."': "指定可执行篮子算例。<bookmark mark='a'/>80美元买一份。<bookmark mark='b'/>假设交付篮子实际毛卖价84，按毛值收2%卖出成本。<bookmark mark='c'/>净额82.32，其他成本前赚{gain:.2f}美元。<bookmark mark='d'/>若公布标记未变而实际毛价仅79，同样成本后只得77.42，亏2.58。例子说明标记净值不一定代表可执行套利。",
    "Two connected roles. <bookmark mark='a'/> Exchange market makers quote ETF shares and may hedge with futures, baskets or related funds. Authorized participants submit primary-market creation or redemption transactions under fund terms, cutoffs and settlement procedures; execution is not simply one universal end-of-day event. <bookmark mark='b'/> A dealer estimates executable fair value and the cost of that route. <bookmark mark='c'/> Authorization usually does not oblige it to arbitrage every discount; capital constraints and basket risks can make a visible gap persist.": "两个相连角色。<bookmark mark='a'/>交易所做市商为份额报价，可用期货、篮子或相关基金对冲。授权参与者按基金条款、截止与结算程序提交一级申赎，并非统一的日末事件。<bookmark mark='b'/>交易商估计可执行公允价值及通道成本。<bookmark mark='c'/>授权通常不要求它对每个折价套利，资本与篮子风险可使差距持续。",
    "Three details that matter. <bookmark mark='a'/> Redeeming in kind lets an American fund hand over low-cost-basis securities instead of selling them, so fewer capital gains reach shareholders. <bookmark mark='b'/> Since the SEC's twenty nineteen ETF rule, funds may accept custom baskets that differ from their holdings, which helps bond funds. <bookmark mark='c'/> And some funds create in cash, so the fund itself trades the securities; the first American spot Bitcoin funds, approved in January twenty twenty-four, were set up that way.": "三个重要的细节。<bookmark mark='a'/>实物赎回让美国基金可以交出成本基础低的证券而不是卖掉它们，所以分配给股东的资本利得更少。<bookmark mark='b'/>自美国证券交易委员会2019年的ETF规则以来，基金可以接受与其持仓不同的定制篮子，这对债券基金有帮助。<bookmark mark='c'/>有些基金以现金申购，由基金自己交易证券；2024年1月获批的首批美国现货比特币基金就是这样设立的。",
    "How the price is watched. <bookmark mark='a'/> Many exchanges publish an indicative value of the basket every fifteen seconds, from its holdings' last prices. <bookmark mark='b'/> The premium is the price over the official value, minus one. <bookmark mark='c'/> But makers do not quote off published values. They build their own fair value from the most liquid related prices, futures and other funds, which is why they can quote a bond fund when the bonds themselves are not trading.": "价格是如何被盯着的。<bookmark mark='a'/>许多交易所每十五秒公布一次篮子的参考价值，来自持仓的最新价格。<bookmark mark='b'/>溢价是价格除以官方净值再减一。<bookmark mark='c'/>但做市商并不按公布的值报价。他们用最具流动性的相关价格，期货和其他基金，构建自己的公允价值，这就是为什么即使债券本身没有交易，他们也能为债券基金报价。",
    "March twenty twenty as a literature case. <bookmark mark='a'/> BIS researchers documented bond ETF dislocations and the difficulty of arbitraging illiquid holdings during stress. <bookmark mark='b'/> A price drawdown and a discount to NAV are different quantities. A close-only series cannot measure the discount, and price response alone cannot identify an announcement's causal effect. <bookmark mark='c'/> A careful study needs synchronized NAV and executable basket information, funding, creation terms and a credible identification design. We use the cited case to explain mechanisms without a new numerical price chart.": "2020年3月作为文献案例。<bookmark mark='a'/>国际清算银行研究者记录压力下债券ETF偏离，以及非流动持仓的套利困难。<bookmark mark='b'/>跨期跌幅与净值折价不同；仅收盘价不能测折价，价格反应也不能单独识别公告因果效果。<bookmark mark='c'/>严谨研究需同步净值、可执行篮子、融资、申赎条款及可信识别设计。这里借所引案例解释机制，没有新的数值价格图。",
    "Interpreting a NAV gap. <bookmark mark='a'/> Evaluated prices for less frequently traded bonds can lag executable values, although infrequent trading does not make every mark stale. <bookmark mark='b'/> Liquid ETF shares can contribute price discovery, while also reflecting their own flow and risk premia. <bookmark mark='c'/> The cited March literature discusses valuation and constrained intermediation channels. Our illustrations do not estimate their separate contributions or show that a particular discount is an error.": "解释净值差距。<bookmark mark='a'/>较少成交债券的评估价可能滞后于可执行值，但成交少不使每个标记都陈旧。<bookmark mark='b'/>流动ETF份额可以参与价格发现，也反映自身资金流与风险溢价。<bookmark mark='c'/>所引3月文献讨论估值与中介约束通道；我们的说明不估计各自贡献，也不证明某个折价是错误。",
    "Keep the chronology precise. <bookmark mark='a'/> The March twenty-third SMCCF term sheet initially specified investment-grade corporate-bond ETFs. <bookmark mark='b'/> The April ninth expansion included high-yield bond ETFs, while retaining a predominant investment-grade allocation. <bookmark mark='c'/> Announcement effects can precede purchases, but an observed recovery alone does not show that dealer balance sheets were restored by that announcement. The official term sheets establish eligibility dates; causal policy studies require additional evidence.": "精确区分时间。<bookmark mark='a'/>3月23日SMCCF条款最初规定投资级公司债ETF。<bookmark mark='b'/>4月9日扩展纳入高收益债ETF，同时保留以投资级为主的分配。<bookmark mark='c'/>公告影响可早于购买，但观察到恢复不能单独证明交易商资产负债表被该公告修复。官方条款确立资格日期，因果政策研究还需额外证据。",
    "Daily leverage resets. <bookmark mark='a'/> In a frictionless single-asset calculation, begin with assets A zero and exposure L times assets, with no subscriptions, financing or tracking costs. <bookmark mark='b'/> After underlying return r, new assets are A zero times one plus L r, while existing exposure is L A zero times one plus r. Their difference gives the required trade L times L minus one times r times A zero. <bookmark mark='c'/> For triple leverage and a five-percent fall, sell thirty percent of beginning-of-day assets in exposure. That is not thirty percent of the reduced ending assets. For leverage between zero and one, the directional statement reverses.": "每日杠杆重置。<bookmark mark='a'/>无摩擦单资产算例以日初资产A零和L倍敞口开始，无申赎、融资或跟踪成本。<bookmark mark='b'/>标的回报r后，新资产为A零乘一加Lr，原敞口为LA零乘一加r。目标与原敞口之差为L乘L减一再乘r和A零。<bookmark mark='c'/>三倍杠杆遇标的跌5%，需卖日初资产30%的敞口，不是日末缩水资产的30%。杠杆在零到一之间时方向关系相反。",
    "Three lessons. <bookmark mark='a'/> The band is a cost, not a law: in stress the cost of balance sheet dominates. <bookmark mark='b'/> For illiquid holdings, the fund's price can be the better one, and a discount can be information. <bookmark mark='c'/> And an ETF offers liquidity on top of assets that have little. It works because market makers warehouse the gap, and it strains when they cannot.": "三条教训。<bookmark mark='a'/>区间是成本，而不是定律：在压力下，资产负债表的成本占主导。<bookmark mark='b'/>对流动性差的持仓，基金的价格可能是更好的价格，折价可能是信息。<bookmark mark='c'/>ETF在流动性很少的资产之上提供流动性。它之所以有效，是因为做市商为这段差距提供仓储，而当他们做不到时，它就承受压力。",
    "Pause and predict. Public news moves Bitcoin's value by ten ticks. A maker's stale quote can be cancelled, or picked off by any of four rivals as fast as it is. With five equally fast firms, how often is it picked off?": '暂停并预测。公开消息让比特币的价值移动十跳。做市商过时的报价可以被撤销，也可能被四个与它一样快的对手中的任何一个狙击。在五家同样快的公司中，它被狙击的频率是多少？',
    'Chapter six, and the answer to the pause: four times in five. When news is public, the maker who quoted is one runner against many, and wins the race to cancel only as often as anyone else wins the race to trade. Eric Budish, Peter Cramton and John Shim turned that into an equilibrium.': '第6章，以及暂停问题的答案：五次中有四次。当消息公开时，报价的做市商是一个对多个的赛跑者，它赢得撤单比赛的频率，只和任何其他人赢得成交比赛的频率一样。Eric Budish、Peter Cramton和John Shim把这变成了一个均衡。',
    "The race. <bookmark mark='a'/> News arrives: a futures price moves, or a correlated asset ticks, public information that every fast firm sees within microseconds. <bookmark mark='b'/> The maker sends a cancel; its rivals send orders to hit the stale quote; the exchange processes messages one at a time, in the order they arrive. <bookmark mark='c'/> With N equally fast firms, the maker's cancel arrives first one time in N.": "赛跑。<bookmark mark='a'/>消息到来：期货价格变动，或者相关资产跳动，每家快速公司都在几微秒内看到的公开信息。<bookmark mark='b'/>做市商发出撤单；它的对手发出订单去打那个过时的报价；交易所按到达顺序逐条处理消息。<bookmark mark='c'/>在N家同样快的公司中，做市商的撤单先到的概率是N分之一。",
    "The simplified role model. Assume at least two equally fast firms, positive investor and public-jump rates, a positive fixed jump, unit uninformed orders and frictionless price undercutting. <bookmark mark='a'/> A provider receives half-spread h from each investor and loses J minus h when a rival beats its cancel, for h below J. <bookmark mark='b'/> Each of the other firms wins with probability one over N. <bookmark mark='c'/> The role-indifference condition cancels N and gives h equal to lambda J times J divided by the sum of rates. This is conditional on the model's trading and competition assumptions.": "简化角色模型。假设至少两家等速企业，投资者和公共跳跃到达率正，固定幅度正，无信息单位订单且可无摩擦压价。<bookmark mark='a'/>提供者从每位投资者收半价差h；h小于J时，竞争者先于撤单则损失J减h。<bookmark mark='b'/>其余每家以一除以N概率先到。<bookmark mark='c'/>角色无差异条件消去N，得h等于跳跃率乘J再除以两速率之和。结论依赖这些交易与竞争假设。",
    'f"Simulate it: investors at rate one, jumps of four at rate a tenth, five firms, a long run. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> As the half-spread widens, the maker\'s profit rises and each sniper\'s falls. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> They cross where the formula says, at {b[\'s_star\']:.2f}. A narrower spread would make makers become snipers; a wider one would draw snipers into making."': "模拟一下：投资者速率为1，大小为4的跳动速率为十分之一，五家公司，长时间运行。<bookmark mark='a'/>随着半价差加宽，做市商的利润上升，每个狙击者的利润下降。<bookmark mark='b'/>它们恰好在公式所说的{b['s_star']:.2f}处相交。更窄的价差会让做市商变成狙击者；更宽的价差会把狙击者吸引来做市。",
    "A consistency check within that model. <bookmark mark='a'/> At the formula's spread, expected provider profit and each sniper's profit are equal for every chosen N. The finite Monte Carlo estimates differ slightly. Each role receives investor payments divided by N; their sum is industry profit. The spread's independence from N holds with the other assumptions fixed and does not describe arbitrary entry or speed investment.": "模型内部一致性检查。<bookmark mark='a'/>在公式价差处，每个选定N下，提供者与每位纯狙击者的预期利润相等，有限蒙特卡洛估计略有差异。每个角色取得投资者支付的N分之一，合计为行业利润。固定其他假设时价差与N无关，不描述任意进入或速度投资。",
    'f"Replay losses in dollar units. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> With a one-bitcoin unit and ten-cent tick, the slow rule\'s final-mid loss is about {slow_k:.0f} thousand dollars on May seventeenth. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> The within-step hindsight variant loses about {fast_k:.0f} thousand. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The numerical gap combines altered fills and inventory paths. It is neither a measured sniping rent nor a causal dollar value of real latency. The replay omits funding, fees, hedging and executable liquidation."': "把回放亏损换成美元。<bookmark mark='a'/>每单位一比特币、每档0.10美元，5月17日慢速规则日终损失约{slow_k:.0f}千美元。<bookmark mark='b'/>步内事后变体约{fast_k:.0f}千美元。<bookmark mark='c'/>差距包含改变的成交筛选与库存路径，既不是测得的狙击租金，也不是实际延迟的因果美元价值。回放还缺资金费、费用、对冲和可执行平仓。",
    "Separate the speed-investment game. <bookmark mark='a'/> Suppose a fixed prize R is split equally among fast firms, with slow firms getting nothing whenever a fast firm exists. If none invests, all share R over N. <bookmark mark='b'/> Investment costs c. With m fast rivals, joining them earns R over m plus one, less c; remaining slow earns zero. <bookmark mark='c'/> For positive c below R over N, investment is strictly dominant. Everyone invests and loses c relative to the all-slow outcome. These explicit assumptions establish a prisoner's dilemma; being faster alone does not prove it.": "另行规定速度投资博弈。<bookmark mark='a'/>假设固定奖池R由快企业平分；只要有快企业，慢者所得为零，无人投资则各得R除以N。<bookmark mark='b'/>投资成本c，有m个快对手时加入可得R除以m加一再减c，保持慢速为零。<bookmark mark='c'/>当正成本低于R除以N，投资严格占优；全投各比全慢少c。这些明确假设才建立囚徒困境，单独跑得更快不能证明它。",
    "External evidence and our proxy have different meanings. <bookmark mark='a'/> Aquilina, Budish and O'Neill used exchange message data to study London latency races and estimate their trading cost. <bookmark mark='b'/> Our hundred-millisecond Bitcoin replay cannot identify such races or convert its selected performance gap into the same structural quantity. <bookmark mark='c'/> Baron and colleagues document concentrated profits and associations with relative speed among observed high-frequency firms. Neither result identifies every benefit or cost of faster markets.": "外部证据与本代理含义不同。<bookmark mark='a'/>阿奎利纳、布迪什和奥尼尔用交易所逐消息数据研究伦敦延迟竞赛并估计交易成本。<bookmark mark='b'/>本100毫秒比特币回放不能识别这种竞赛，也不能把筛选表现差距换成同一结构量。<bookmark mark='c'/>巴伦等记录所观测高频企业中利润集中及相对速度关联；两类结果都不识别快速市场的全部收益或成本。",
    'f"The physics of the race. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The futures exchanges near Chicago and the stock exchanges near New York are about eleven hundred and fifty kilometres apart. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Light in air covers that in about {t_air:.1f} milliseconds. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> In glass fibre, slowed by its refractive index, about {t_fibre:.1f}. <bookmark mark=\'d\'/> The difference, under two milliseconds, is what paid for chains of microwave towers between the two cities: a calculation from physics, not any firm\'s measured route."': "比赛的物理学。<bookmark mark='a'/>芝加哥附近的期货交易所和纽约附近的股票交易所相距约一千一百五十公里。<bookmark mark='b'/>光在空气中走完这段约需{t_air:.1f}毫秒。<bookmark mark='c'/>在被折射率减慢的玻璃光纤中，约需{t_fibre:.1f}毫秒。<bookmark mark='d'/>两者之差不到两毫秒，正是这一差距支付了两座城市之间的微波塔链：这是根据物理学的计算，而不是任何公司测得的线路。",
    "Design proposals. <bookmark mark='a'/> Uniform-price batches can permit quote updates and price competition within an interval; stale execution can remain near its boundary or with asymmetric information. <bookmark mark='b'/> IEX introduced a three-hundred-and-fifty-microsecond access delay and mechanisms to protect certain pegged orders. Details depend on the order type and rule version. <bookmark mark='c'/> Asymmetric delays and messaging fees change incentives too. Their welfare requires modeling information, participation and routing, rather than assuming every speed expense is waste.": "设计建议。<bookmark mark='a'/>统一价格批量允许区间内更新报价及价格竞争，但边界附近或信息不对称时仍可有陈旧执行。<bookmark mark='b'/>IEX引入350微秒接入延迟及保护某些挂钩订单的机制，细节依赖订单种类与规则版本。<bookmark mark='c'/>非对称延迟和消息费用也改变激励。福利需建模信息、参与和路由，不能假设每笔速度支出都是浪费。",
    "An illustrative uniform-price auction. <bookmark mark='a'/> Aggregate bids by limit price. <bookmark mark='b'/> Aggregate offers in the same way. <bookmark mark='c'/> At a hundred dollars and one cent, demand is eight and supply six, so six units trade; nearby candidate prices trade fewer units. Better-priced bids receive priority: all three units at a hundred and two cents, then three of the five marginal bid units, rationed pro rata under our chosen rule. This allocation rule is an assumption, not universal across auctions.": "说明性的统一价格拍卖。<bookmark mark='a'/>按限价汇总买单。<bookmark mark='b'/>卖单同样处理。<bookmark mark='c'/>100.01美元处需求八、供应六，成交六单位；附近候选价格成交更少。优价买单优先，100.02的三单位全成交，再按指定比例规则分配边际价五单位中的三单位。这个分配规则是题设，不是所有拍卖都如此。",
    "Why it has not happened. <bookmark mark='a'/> Budish, Robin Lee and Shim argue that exchanges earn from selling speed, colocation and data, and have little private reason to switch. <bookmark mark='b'/> Batching has costs too: liquidity fragments if one venue batches alone, the interval must be chosen, and new games appear at the batch boundary. <bookmark mark='c'/> And batching already exists, in opening and closing auctions: doing it ten times a second is the novelty.": "为什么还没有实现。<bookmark mark='a'/>Budish、Robin Lee和Shim认为，交易所靠出售速度，即托管和数据，赚钱，几乎没有自己切换的动机。<bookmark mark='b'/>批量拍卖也有成本：如果只有一个场所批量化，流动性会分散；批次间隔必须选择；批次边界上会出现新的博弈。<bookmark mark='c'/>批量拍卖其实早已存在，就是开盘和收盘集合竞价：每秒做十次才是新东西。",
    'Pause and predict. If a market switched to batch auctions every tenth of a second, what would happen to the sniping prize, to the spread, and to the value of being a microsecond faster?': '暂停并预测。如果一个市场改为每十分之一秒进行一次批量拍卖，狙击奖金、价差以及快一微秒的价值会发生什么？',
    "The batch question, conditionally. <bookmark mark='a'/> Ideal common-information repricing before clearing removes the stale-quote prize by assumption. <bookmark mark='b'/> Inventory, private information, fees and participation can still support a positive spread. <bookmark mark='c'/> With finite latency, a small speed difference can matter near the boundary. How much it matters requires an explicit information and update model, which the binary batch flag does not supply.": "有条件回答批量问题。<bookmark mark='a'/>共同信息下清算前理想重定价，按假设删除陈旧报价奖池。<bookmark mark='b'/>库存、私人信息、费用和参与仍可支持正价差。<bookmark mark='c'/>有限延迟下，小速度差可在边界重要。其大小需要明确信息与更新模型，二元批量标志没有提供。",
    "Chapter seven. A handful of studies have seen inside high-frequency firms' trading through regulators' data. They tell a consistent story about where the money comes from, and who keeps it.": '第7章。少数几项研究通过监管者的数据看到了高频公司的交易内部。它们讲述了一个一致的故事：钱从哪里来，谁留住了它。',
    "An attributed case study. <bookmark mark='a'/> Menkveld examined one large high-frequency market maker trading on Chi-X and Euronext and documented spread and rebate revenues. <bookmark mark='b'/> Its positioning component was negative in the study's decomposition. <bookmark mark='c'/> Net profit was positive with high turnover and actively managed inventory. This is one firm's observed business, not our coarse-grid replay made profitable merely by substituting a faster label.": "一个署名案例研究。<bookmark mark='a'/>门克韦尔德研究在Chi-X与泛欧交易所交易的一家大型高频做市商，记录价差和返佣收入。<bookmark mark='b'/>按该研究的分解，头寸成分为负。<bookmark mark='c'/>高周转及主动库存管理下净利润正。这是一家公司的观测业务，不是把我们的粗网格回放贴上快速标签就变成盈利。",
    "Across firms. <bookmark mark='a'/> High-frequency firms both make and take liquidity, and Baron and colleagues found the aggressive, liquidity-taking ones among the most profitable. <bookmark mark='b'/> Profits concentrate in the fastest few; new entrants earn less and exit more often. <bookmark mark='c'/> And what predicts profit is rank in speed, not speed itself: the asset is being faster than everyone else, the arms race of Chapter six.": "跨公司来看。<bookmark mark='a'/>高频公司既挂单也吃单，Baron和同事发现，激进的、吃单的那些是最赚钱的之一。<bookmark mark='b'/>利润集中在最快的少数几家；新进入者赚得更少，退出得更频繁。<bookmark mark='c'/>预测利润的是速度排名，而不是速度本身：资产在于比所有人都快，也就是第6章的军备竞赛。",
    "What speed uses. <bookmark mark='a'/> Colocation, feeds and technical staff have fixed and variable costs. <bookmark mark='b'/> Faster intercity links use real resources. <bookmark mark='c'/> Hardware logic can reduce processing latency. The fixed-prize toy game treats this spending as redundant. In a broader market, technology may also improve reliability, hedging or price discovery, so its entire cost is not automatically social waste.": "速度耗用什么。<bookmark mark='a'/>托管、数据流与技术人员有固定及可变成本。<bookmark mark='b'/>更快城际链路消耗真实资源。<bookmark mark='c'/>硬件逻辑可减少处理延迟。固定奖池玩具博弈把这种支出视为冗余；更广市场中，技术也可能改善可靠性、对冲和价格发现，所以其全部成本不自动是社会浪费。",
    "How inventory is really managed. <bookmark mark='a'/> A maker in many names accumulates small positions everywhere. <bookmark mark='b'/> The common factor is hedged at once in the most liquid instrument, an index future: Part thirty-one's risk model in real time. <bookmark mark='c'/> What remains is small and specific to each name, and is shed by skewing quotes, the way Menkveld's maker unwound within minutes.": "存货实际上如何管理。<bookmark mark='a'/>为许多标的做市的公司会在各处积累小仓位。<bookmark mark='b'/>共同因子立即在流动性最好的工具，即股指期货上对冲：实时版的第31部分风险模型。<bookmark mark='c'/>剩下的部分很小，属于各个标的，通过倾斜报价来甩掉，就像Menkveld那家做市商在几分钟内平仓一样。",
    "In stress. <bookmark mark='a'/> In normal times, competition among fast makers has narrowed spreads in most markets. <bookmark mark='b'/> When volatility jumps, so do adverse selection and inventory risk, and makers widen or withdraw, as on the sixth of May twenty ten and the fifteenth of October twenty fourteen. <bookmark mark='c'/> Most electronic makers are not obliged to quote. Liquidity supplied by choice can be withdrawn by choice.": "在压力之下。<bookmark mark='a'/>平常时期，快速做市商之间的竞争让大多数市场的价差变窄。<bookmark mark='b'/>当波动率跳升，逆向选择和存货风险也跳升，做市商加宽报价或撤离，就像2010年5月6日和2014年10月15日那样。<bookmark mark='c'/>大多数电子做市商没有报价义务。出于选择提供的流动性，也可以出于选择撤走。",
    "Quoting obligations depend on jurisdiction and role. <bookmark mark='a'/> MiFID two established agreement and quoting requirements for covered algorithmic market-making strategies, subject to its definitions and exceptions. <bookmark mark='b'/> American designated-maker and exchange programs have venue-specific requirements and incentives. <bookmark mark='c'/> Such rules can support continuity but do not guarantee unlimited liquidity in stress. This is an institutional overview, not a current legal compliance test or a claim that every electronic firm has the same obligations.": "报价义务因管辖及角色而异。<bookmark mark='a'/>欧盟MiFID二为符合定义的算法做市策略设协议与报价要求，并有相应例外。<bookmark mark='b'/>美国指定做市商和交易所项目各有规则与激励。<bookmark mark='c'/>义务可支持连续性，但不保证压力下无限流动性。这里是制度概览，不是当前法律合规测试，也不声称每家电子企业义务相同。",
    "Interpreting the measured race prize. <bookmark mark='a'/> Aquilina, Budish and O'Neill extrapolated their London estimate to a multi-billion-dollar global equity figure, with the study's sampling and scaling assumptions. <bookmark mark='b'/> Race winners receive transfers that can affect investor costs and firms' incentives. <bookmark mark='c'/> The transfer itself is not automatically a deadweight social loss. Resource spending, liquidity and information effects require a separate welfare analysis.": "解释测得的竞赛奖池。<bookmark mark='a'/>阿奎利纳、布迪什和奥尼尔按研究抽样与外推假设，把伦敦估计扩展至全球股票数十亿美元量级。<bookmark mark='b'/>获胜者取得转移收入，会影响投资者成本与企业激励。<bookmark mark='c'/>转移本身不是自动的社会无谓损失，资源支出、流动性和信息效果需要另作福利分析。",
    "Options at scale. <bookmark mark='a'/> An options maker quotes every strike and expiry from one volatility surface, so a move in the surface reprices them all at once. <bookmark mark='b'/> Its inventory is its Greeks: delta hedged continuously, vega and gamma managed by skewing quotes. <bookmark mark='c'/> And it runs the same race: a stale surface is sniped like a stale quote, thousands of prices at a time.": "大规模的期权做市。<bookmark mark='a'/>期权做市商用一个波动率曲面为每个行权价和到期日报价，所以曲面一动，所有报价同时重新定价。<bookmark mark='b'/>它的存货就是它的希腊字母：持续对冲delta，通过倾斜报价管理vega和gamma。<bookmark mark='c'/>它也参加同样的比赛：过时的曲面像过时的报价一样被狙击，一次成千上万个价格。",
    "Crypto market-making costs. <bookmark mark='a'/> Volume tiers and contractual rebates change fees, but our chosen replay rebate arithmetic does not show a viable professional business. <bookmark mark='b'/> Cross-venue hedging adds basis, funding, collateral and counterparty risks absent from the single-book reconstruction. <bookmark mark='c'/> Token-issuer contracts can also create conflicts. Specific enforcement findings must be attributed to their cases rather than generalized to every maker.": "加密做市成本。<bookmark mark='a'/>成交量分层及合同返佣改变费用，但指定回放的返佣算术不能证明可行的专业业务。<bookmark mark='b'/>跨场所对冲增加单簿重建未计的基差、资金费、抵押和对手方风险。<bookmark mark='c'/>代币发行方合同也可产生冲突；具体执法结论应归属具体案件，不能推广到所有做市商。",
    "Pause and predict. The House wants to make markets in Bitcoin's perpetual. Given Chapters two to six, what three things must its desk have before it posts a single order?": '暂停并预测。本系列公司想为比特币永续合约做市。根据第2章到第6章，它的交易台在挂出第一笔订单之前必须具备哪三样东西？',
    "The proposed desk standard. <bookmark mark='a'/> Estimate horizon-consistent marked edge after rebates and all trading costs, using the desk's actual fills and decision-time information. Markout is not an extra loss to subtract again from a complete inventory ledger. <bookmark mark='b'/> Measure latency and queue treatment rather than treating our hindsight variant as a speed estimate. <bookmark mark='c'/> Specify position and loss limits, monitoring and a kill switch. These are research requirements, not deployment approval.": "拟议交易台标准。<bookmark mark='a'/>使用自己的实际成交及决策时点信息，估计同一时限下、计返佣与全部成本的标记边际。不利标记不能从完整库存账本再次扣除。<bookmark mark='b'/>测量延迟与队列处理，不把事后变体当速度估计。<bookmark mark='c'/>规定头寸及损失上限、监测和停机开关。这些是研究要求，不是部署批准。",
    'Chapter eight. Rule thirty-eight is a proposed research standard for a market-making desk, not evidence that the House has launched one. Quoting can accumulate losses rapidly, so risk controls and accounting must be specified before any deployment decision.': '第8章。第38条是做市交易台的拟议研究标准，不是量化之家已经开业的证据。报价可以迅速累积损失，因此任何部署决策前，都要规定控制和核算。',
    "The proposed research sheet. <bookmark mark='a'/> Five audited ordinary outputs support the Bitcoin replay, reach proxies, GLFT approximation and sniping illustrations. The touch rules lose on their specified final-mid ledger. Far reach marks can be positive without defining an executable portfolio. The sub-tick sniping root is a model substitution. The bond ETF example is qualitative and sourced; it has no fresh price or NAV statistic.": "拟议研究表。<bookmark mark='a'/>五个经审计常规输出支持比特币回放、触达代理、GLFT近似和狙击说明。最优价规则在指定日终账本亏损，远档触达毛标记可能为正但未定义可执行组合。低于一档的狙击根只是代入模型。债券ETF案例定性且有文献来源，没有新的价格或净值统计。",
    "Controls, before any edge. <bookmark mark='a'/> Position limits per instrument and in total, each with its hedge. <bookmark mark='b'/> Loss limits, and a switch that stops quoting automatically when losses, messages or fills move faster than expected. <bookmark mark='c'/> And pre-trade checks on every order, price collars and size limits, which in the United States the Market Access Rule requires of broker-dealers.": "先有控制，再谈优势。<bookmark mark='a'/>每个工具和总体的仓位上限，各自配有对冲。<bookmark mark='b'/>亏损上限，以及在亏损、消息或成交比预期更快时自动停止报价的开关。<bookmark mark='c'/>还有对每笔订单的交易前检查，价格区间和数量上限，在美国，市场准入规则要求经纪自营商这样做。",
    "A possible validation sequence. <bookmark mark='a'/> First a past-only replay with measured latency, conservative queue assumptions and all execution costs. <bookmark mark='b'/> A separately authorized small live experiment could compare realized fills and marks with predeclared predictions. That difference includes model error and changing market conditions. <bookmark mark='c'/> Scaling would require independently reviewed uncertainty, controls and capital. None of these deployment experiments or approvals is performed in this lesson.": "可能的验证顺序。<bookmark mark='a'/>先仅用过去信息回放，含实测延迟、保守队列假设及全部执行成本。<bookmark mark='b'/>另经授权的小额实盘实验，可把实际成交和标记与预先声明的预测比较；差距包含模型误差及市场条件变化。<bookmark mark='c'/>扩容需独立审阅不确定性、控制与资本。本课没有执行这些部署实验或审批。",
    "Capital and liquidity requirements. <bookmark mark='a'/> Perpetual and derivative positions require venue collateral; spot inventory also ties up funds and can have financing or settlement requirements. <bookmark mark='b'/> A stress budget needs adverse scenarios for one-sided fills, hedge slippage, funding and venue access, rather than a claim that one observed worst minute sets capital. <bookmark mark='c'/> Proposed quoting size must fit those scenarios, limits and execution assumptions. This part performs no capital approval.": "资本和流动性要求。<bookmark mark='a'/>永续及衍生品需场所抵押，现货库存也占用资金，可能涉及融资或结算要求。<bookmark mark='b'/>压力预算需考虑单边成交、对冲滑点、资金费和场所访问的不利情形，不能说一个观测最差分钟就决定资本。<bookmark mark='c'/>拟议报价规模须适应这些情景、限制及执行假设；本部分不进行资本审批。",
    "Chapter three's measurement. For each second, the furthest any buy reached above the starting mid, and any sell below it, in ticks; then, for each distance, the share of seconds that reached it.": '第3章的测量。对每一秒，记录任何买单超过起始中间价的最远距离，以及任何卖单低于它的最远距离，以跳为单位；然后对每个距离，计算达到它的秒的比例。',
    "Chapter one's closed form, in four lines: the skew constant from volatility, risk aversion and the fill parameters, and the half-spread as the base term plus half the skew.": '第1章的闭式解，四行：由波动率、风险厌恶和成交参数算出的倾斜常数，以及等于基础项加半个倾斜的半价差。',
    'The unchanged replay excerpt. With the fast flag, it knows whether any trade in the current grid step passes through the quote and discards that fill. Otherwise a through-price trade, or at-price volume strictly exceeding reconstructed ahead quantity, fills one unit. This is an assumed event reconstruction with hindsight, not an implementable cancellation policy.': '未改动回放片段。快速标志知道当前网格步是否有成交穿过报价，并删除该次执行；否则穿价或同价成交量严格超过重建前方数量时执行一单位。这是带事后信息的事件重建假设，不是可实施撤单策略。',
    'The unchanged sniping source. The closed-form root solves the stipulated role comparison. The simulation allocates jump races using one over N random priority. Setting a batch flag removes those stale trades by construction; the numerical batch interval is unused, so it cannot validate the separate finite-latency formulas.': '未改动狙击源码。闭式根解决规定的角色比较；模拟按一除以N随机优先分配跳跃竞赛。批量标志按构造删除陈旧交易，数值批长未使用，所以不能验证另行给出的有限延迟公式。',
    "Two desks under one roof. <bookmark mark='a'/> When the portfolio desk's order could trade against the market-making desk's inventory, crossing it inside the House saves both sides the spread. <bookmark mark='b'/> But the maker would see the executor's flow, and trading ahead of it would be front-running its own client. <bookmark mark='c'/> So the desks are separated, crossing happens only at a price fixed by the public market, and compliance reviews every case.": "同一屋檐下的两个交易台。<bookmark mark='a'/>当组合台的订单可以与做市台的存货成交时，在本系列公司内部撮合能为双方省下价差。<bookmark mark='b'/>但做市商会看到执行者的订单流，抢在它之前交易就是抢跑自己的客户。<bookmark mark='c'/>所以两个台是分开的，内部撮合只能以公开市场确定的价格进行，合规部门审查每一个案例。",
    "The proposed toolkit. <bookmark mark='a'/> Reach measurements, an approximate quoting model, a reconstructed maker replay and simplified sniping functions. <bookmark mark='b'/> Rule thirty-eight asks for one consistent horizon-specific edge calculation, actual latency and queue treatment, all costs, uncertainty, capital and kill-switch controls. ETF trades require executable baskets and financing under stress. The House has not deployed or approved these strategies; the tools are research building blocks.": "拟议工具包。<bookmark mark='a'/>触达测量、近似报价模型、重建做市回放及简化狙击函数。<bookmark mark='b'/>第38条要求一致的指定时限边际、实际延迟和队列处理、全部成本、不确定性、资本与停机控制。ETF交易需压力下可执行篮子和融资。量化之家未部署或批准这些策略，工具只是研究积木。",
    "The rule against three cases. <bookmark mark='a'/> A backtest of a quoting strategy: ask how fills were simulated, at the back of the queue or the front, and whether sweeps were counted. <bookmark mark='b'/> A vendor's optimal-quote model: ask for its markouts, not its fill rates. <bookmark mark='c'/> An ETF arbitrage that always works: ask what happens when the bonds cannot be sold at their published value, and whose balance sheet holds them.": "用三个案例检验这条规则。<bookmark mark='a'/>一份报价策略的回测：问成交是怎样模拟的，排在队列末尾还是前面，扫单有没有计入。<bookmark mark='b'/>供应商的最优报价模型：要它的事后损益，而不是成交率。<bookmark mark='c'/>一个总能成功的ETF套利：问当债券无法按公布价值卖出时会发生什么，以及由谁的资产负债表来持有它们。",
    'For the researcher. We derive a unique role-indifference spread under a simplified equal-speed model and extend its root equation to integrable random jump magnitudes. We distinguish industry revenue from transfers to pure snipers. A batch exposure heuristic and an explicit speed-investment game are separate models. Simulation checks arithmetic under the source assumptions; it does not prove market-wide welfare or identify public news from Bitcoin snapshots.': '写给研究者。在简化等速模型下推导唯一角色无差异价差，再扩展到可积随机跳幅的根方程。区分行业收入与纯狙击者转移。批量暴露启发式和明确速度投资博弈属于另两个模型。模拟只在源码假设内检查算术，不证明全市场福利，也不从比特币快照识别公共新闻。',
    "The assumptions. <bookmark mark='a'/> Public value has symmetric fixed jumps of positive size J at positive rate lambda J. <bookmark mark='b'/> Independent uninformed investors arrive at positive rate lambda I and trade one unit. <bookmark mark='c'/> At least two identical-speed, risk-neutral firms have simultaneous messages ordered uniformly at random. <bookmark mark='d'/> One quotes around value and others can snipe or undercut continuously, with no tick, inventory, fees or investment cost. The conclusion is limited to this role model.": "模型假设。<bookmark mark='a'/>公共价值以正速率发生正幅度J的对称跳跃。<bookmark mark='b'/>独立无信息投资者按正速率到达，每次一单位。<bookmark mark='c'/>至少两家风险中性等速企业，同时消息按均匀随机顺序处理。<bookmark mark='d'/>一家围绕价值报价，其余可狙击或连续压价；没有价位、库存、费用或投资成本。结论限于此角色模型。",
    "Lemma one, the payoffs. <bookmark mark='a'/> The provider earns from every investor, and loses whenever one of the other N minus one messages beats its cancel. <bookmark mark='b'/> Each other firm wins a given race one time in N. <bookmark mark='c'/> And the difference between the two roles does not contain N at all: the provider's losses and one sniper's gains add up to one whole race per jump.": "引理一，收益。<bookmark mark='a'/>提供者从每个投资者那里赚钱，每当其他N减一条消息中有一条先于它的撤单，它就亏钱。<bookmark mark='b'/>其他每家公司赢得某场比赛的概率是N分之一。<bookmark mark='c'/>两种角色之间的差完全不含N：提供者的损失和一个狙击者的收益加起来，正好是每次跳动一整场比赛。",
    "Lemma two, indifference. <bookmark mark='a'/> If providing paid more than sniping, a rival would post a slightly narrower spread, take the investors, and earn more: competition on price. <bookmark mark='b'/> If it paid less, the provider would rather snipe, and no one would provide at that spread. <bookmark mark='c'/> So in any equilibrium the two roles are equally attractive.": "引理二，无差异。<bookmark mark='a'/>如果提供流动性比狙击赚得多，对手就会挂出稍窄一点的价差，拿走投资者，赚得更多：价格竞争。<bookmark mark='b'/>如果赚得少，提供者宁愿去狙击，在那个价差上就没有人提供流动性。<bookmark mark='c'/>所以在任何均衡中，两种角色同样有吸引力。",
    "Existence and uniqueness of the indifference root. <bookmark mark='a'/> Let D of h be investor revenue minus the jump excess rate. <bookmark mark='b'/> With positive rates and positive J, it is negative at zero and positive at J. Continuity gives a root. It increases by at least lambda I times any increase in h, so the root is unique. <bookmark mark='c'/> Inside zero to J, solve the linear equation. This establishes the unique candidate spread under the prior role and undercutting assumptions, not a complete endogenous-speed equilibrium.": "无差异根的存在与唯一。<bookmark mark='a'/>D关于h为投资者收入减跳跃超额速率。<bookmark mark='b'/>正速率及正J下，零处负、J处正，连续性给根。h每增加一段，D至少增加投资者速率乘该段，所以唯一。<bookmark mark='c'/>零至J之间解线性方程。这建立先前角色及压价假设下的唯一候选价差，不是完整内生速度均衡。",
    "The conditional result. <bookmark mark='a'/> The unique half-spread is independent of N when rates, jump sizes and the stated market design are fixed. <bookmark mark='b'/> Each of the N roles earns investor payments divided by N. Industry profit therefore equals all investor spread payments, while the N minus one pure snipers receive only N minus one over N of that amount. Sniping transfers cancel inside the industry's accounts. A separate investment game is needed to discuss speed spending.": "条件结论。<bookmark mark='a'/>固定速率、跳幅及指定设计时，唯一半价差与N无关。<bookmark mark='b'/>N个角色各赚投资者支付的N分之一。行业利润因此等于全部投资者价差支付，而N减一位纯狙击者只取得其N减一除以N。行业内部核算中，狙击转移相消。讨论速度支出仍需独立投资博弈。",
    "Comparative statics with other inputs fixed. <bookmark mark='a'/> A higher public-jump rate increases this model's spread. This alone says nothing about which real correlated markets are sniped most. <bookmark mark='b'/> A higher uninformed investor rate lowers the spread for a fixed jump process and unit size. <bookmark mark='c'/> N cancels only under the equal-speed role structure. Entry can affect other parameters in real markets.": "其他输入固定时的比较静态。<bookmark mark='a'/>公共跳跃率提高会加宽本模型价差，但不能单独说明现实中哪些相关市场最常遭狙击。<bookmark mark='b'/>固定跳跃过程与单位数量时，无信息投资者率提高会降低价差。<bookmark mark='c'/>只有指定等速角色结构中N才抵消；现实进入可改变其他参数。",
    "Random magnitudes U. <bookmark mark='a'/> Assume U is nonnegative, integrable, and positive with positive probability, with both arrival rates positive. The indifference equation uses the expected positive excess U minus h. <bookmark mark='b'/> The left side increases strictly; the excess is continuous and nonincreasing, bounded above by the finite mean. Thus there is exactly one positive root. <bookmark mark='c'/> If one magnitude distribution dominates another in convex order, its expected excess is no smaller at every h, so its root is no smaller. Equal mean and higher variance alone, or a generic fat-tail label, does not imply this ordering.": "随机幅度U。<bookmark mark='a'/>假设U非负、可积，且以正概率为正，两到达率也正。无差异方程使用U减h的正部期望。<bookmark mark='b'/>左侧严格增，超额项连续非增且受有限均值控制，因此恰有一个正根。<bookmark mark='c'/>若一个幅度分布在凸序上支配另一个，其每个h处超额期望不小，根也不小。同均值且更大方差，或笼统厚尾标签，都不保证这种排序。",
    'f"An arithmetic consistency check. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The fixed-jump formula gives {b[\'s_star\']:.3f}. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Interpolating simulated profit differences gives {cross:.3f}. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Across the selected N values, the role means are approximately equal within Monte Carlo variation. This simulation implements the stipulated race probabilities; it does not independently validate an equilibrium in observed markets."': "算术一致性检查。<bookmark mark='a'/>固定幅度公式给{b['s_star']:.3f}。<bookmark mark='b'/>插值模拟利润差给{cross:.3f}。<bookmark mark='c'/>指定N各值下，角色均值在蒙特卡洛波动内约相等。模拟实现规定竞赛概率，并非独立验证观测市场的均衡。",
    'f"What the batch flag actually tests. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> At the continuous-market spread, the five-firm simulation gives roughly {b[\'byN\'][2][\'sniper\']:.3f} per pure sniper per time unit. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> With the batch flag, stale-trade losses are removed by construction. The numeric interval is not used in the unchanged algorithm, and there is no modeled cancellation latency. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> The provider retains investor payments at this fixed spread. The program does not simulate entry, undercutting, the new equilibrium spread or a latency-to-interval law."': "批量标志实际检验什么。<bookmark mark='a'/>在连续市场价差处，五家模拟每位纯狙击者单位时间约赚{b['byN'][2]['sniper']:.3f}。<bookmark mark='b'/>打开批量标志，陈旧交易损失按构造移除；未改动算法不使用数值间隔，也没建模撤单延迟。<bookmark mark='c'/>固定价差下，提供者保留投资者支付。程序没有模拟进入、压价、新均衡价差或延迟与间隔关系。",
    "The ideal repricing argument. <bookmark mark='a'/> If all providers receive public news and can replace quotes before uniform-price clearing, earlier messages within that batch need not win stale trades. <bookmark mark='b'/> With multiple providers, common information and negligible costs, competition can narrow the spread. <bookmark mark='c'/> Real latency, batch-boundary news, private information, inventory and fragmentation remain. Zero stale trades in our flagged simulation are an imposed mechanism, not a proof that every batch design eliminates those costs.": "理想重定价论证。<bookmark mark='a'/>若所有提供者在统一价格清算前都收到公共新闻并可替换报价，批内先到消息不一定赢得陈旧成交。<bookmark mark='b'/>多家、共同信息、可忽略成本下，竞争可缩小价差。<bookmark mark='c'/>现实延迟、边界新闻、私人信息、库存及分散仍在。标志模拟里零陈旧成交是规定机制，不证明所有批量设计都消除这些成本。",
    "A separate exposure heuristic. <bookmark mark='a'/> Assume news has uniform phase in a batch and a deterministic quote-update latency delta. Only the final delta of an interval tau is unprotected when delta is below tau, giving an exposure fraction delta over tau. This is not yet the probability a sniper wins. <bookmark mark='b'/> If we also preserve the same conditional race and role assumptions, replacing the jump-opportunity rate by that fraction gives this illustrative root. <bookmark mark='c'/> One microsecond over one hundred milliseconds is ten to the minus five for opportunities. The spread ratio has a further rate-dependent factor. Our unchanged simulator does not test this latency model.": "独立的暴露启发式。<bookmark mark='a'/>假设新闻在批内相位均匀、报价更新延迟固定为德尔塔。当延迟小于批长时，只有最后德尔塔时间未保护，暴露比例为延迟除以批长，这还不是狙击者胜率。<bookmark mark='b'/>再保留同样条件竞赛和角色假设，以该比例缩放跳跃机会率，可得说明性根。<bookmark mark='c'/>一微秒除以100毫秒为十的负五次方，只针对机会。价差比还有到达率修正因子，未改动模拟没有检验此延迟模型。",
    'f"Separate transfers from resource costs. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Investor spread payments equal industry profit in this simplified model, not profit of the pure snipers alone. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> With the chosen rates, payments are {b[\'lam_i\'] * h:.3f} per time unit. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> Narrower spreads can transfer surplus from firms to investors. Real resources spent on otherwise redundant speed can be a social loss, but adding the entire investor payment again would double-count a transfer. Welfare also depends on participation, information and trading benefits absent from this calculation."': "分开转移与资源成本。<bookmark mark='a'/>简化模型中，投资者价差支付等于行业利润，不是纯狙击者利润。<bookmark mark='b'/>指定速率下，每时间单位支付{b['lam_i'] * h:.3f}。<bookmark mark='c'/>更窄价差可把剩余从企业转给投资者；冗余速度耗用的真实资源可能是社会损失，但再加全部投资者支付会把转移重复计为无谓成本。福利还取决于此处未计的参与、信息和交易收益。",
    "Prove dominance in the separate fixed-prize game. <bookmark mark='a'/> If no rival invests, becoming the sole fast firm gains R times one minus one over N, less cost c. <bookmark mark='b'/> With m fast rivals, remaining slow gets zero, while investing gets R over m plus one, less c. <bookmark mark='c'/> The smallest gross gain across these cases is R over N. Thus positive cost below R over N makes investment strictly dominant. Every firm then gets R over N minus c, worse than the all-slow outcome by c. Total resource use is N c under these explicit assumptions.": "证明独立固定奖池博弈的占优。<bookmark mark='a'/>无人投资时，付每时间成本c成为唯一快者，增益为R乘一减一除以N再减c。<bookmark mark='b'/>有m个快对手时，保持慢速为零，加入得R除以m加一再减c。<bookmark mark='c'/>所有情况中最小毛增益为R除以N，所以正成本低于它时投资严格占优。全投各得R除以N减c，比全慢少c，指定假设下资源总耗用为Nc。",
    'f"Check three: the general condition, with Bitcoin\'s own jump sizes. Simulate the market with jumps drawn from every real mid change and the takers\' real rate. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> The difference between the two roles crosses zero at {cross:.2f} of a tick, <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> where the condition, solved directly, puts it: {b[\'btc\'][\'general_half\']:.2f}."': "检验三：一般条件，使用比特币自己的跳动大小。用从每一次真实中间价变化中抽取的跳动和吃单者的真实速率来模拟市场。<bookmark mark='a'/>两种角色之差在{cross:.2f}跳处穿过零，<bookmark mark='b'/>恰是直接求解该条件所得的位置：{b['btc']['general_half']:.2f}。",
    'f"A proxy substitution, not identification. <bookmark mark=\'a\'/> Net mid changes occur {bt[\'lam_all\']:.2f} times per second in the snapshots, averaging {bt[\'mean_move\']:.0f} ticks. <bookmark mark=\'b\'/> Treating their empirical magnitudes as independent public jumps and aggregate trade counts as uninformed unit arrivals gives a root {bt[\'general_half\']:.2f} tick. <bookmark mark=\'c\'/> That is below the quoted half-tick floor in this model. Snapshots combine endogenous order flow and news, traders have different sizes and information, and jumps are dependent. The result neither identifies the actual natural spread nor attributes the replay losses to another channel."': "代入代理，而非识别。<bookmark mark='a'/>快照中净中点变化每秒{bt['lam_all']:.2f}次，平均{bt['mean_move']:.0f}档。<bookmark mark='b'/>把经验幅度当独立公共跳跃、把归集笔数当无信息单位到达，得到根{bt['general_half']:.2f}档。<bookmark mark='c'/>低于本模型的报价半档下限。快照混合内生流和新闻，交易者数量和信息不同，跳跃也有依赖。结果既不识别真实自然价差，也不把回放亏损归因于其他通道。",
    "Where this sits. <bookmark mark='a'/> Budish, Cramton and Shim's paper has general jumps, the arms race, and batch auctions, with evidence from correlated futures and funds. <bookmark mark='b'/> Aquilina, Budish and O'Neill measured the races on the London Stock Exchange. <bookmark mark='c'/> And Markus Baldauf and Joshua Mollner, and Menkveld and Marius Zoican, showed that once acquiring information is a choice, faster markets can widen spreads or narrow them.": "这项工作的位置。<bookmark mark='a'/>布迪什、克兰顿与希姆论文讨论一般跳幅、速度竞赛和批量拍卖，并研究相关期货与基金。<bookmark mark='b'/>阿奎利纳、布迪什与奥尼尔在伦敦逐消息测量竞赛。<bookmark mark='c'/>巴尔道夫与莫尔纳，以及门克韦尔德与佐伊坎的模型说明，当信息获取内生时，更快市场可能加宽或缩窄价差。",
    "Three open questions. <bookmark mark='a'/> An equilibrium spread with private information, public jumps and inventory together, estimated from message data. <bookmark mark='b'/> When continuous and batch markets coexist, where does liquidity go, and is the result efficient? <bookmark mark='c'/> And sniping across crypto's many venues, with different latencies and no consolidated quote: who wins, and what does it cost takers?": "三个开放问题。<bookmark mark='a'/>同时包含私人信息、公开跳动和存货的均衡价差，并用消息数据估计。<bookmark mark='b'/>当连续市场和批量市场并存时，流动性去哪里，结果是否有效率？<bookmark mark='c'/>以及在加密市场的众多场所之间，延迟各不相同、没有合并报价时的狙击：谁赢，吃单者付出什么？",
    'Pause and predict. Investors arrive at rate ten and jumps of three ticks at rate two. What is the sniping half-spread? And if the jumps are one or five ticks with equal chance, the same mean?': '暂停并预测。投资者以速率10到达，三跳的跳动以速率2到达。狙击半价差是多少？如果跳动以相同概率是一跳或五跳，均值相同呢？',
    'Part thirty-eight, recapped. Marked wealth uses execution edge, rebates and inventory gains. A horizon mark is another view, not an additional loss in that ledger. Our coarse-grid touch replay loses, with different selected fills under hindsight and filtering. Reach probabilities produce equivalent rates, not queue fills. Model quotes and far reach marks are illustrations with omitted execution and inventory costs. Tick constraints change price and priority incentives.': '回顾第38部分。标记财富使用执行边际、返佣和库存收益。时限标记是另一观察，不是账本里的额外损失。粗网格最优价回放亏损，事后信息和过滤选择不同成交。触达概率产生等效速率，不是队列成交。模型报价及远档触达标记是遗漏执行和库存成本的说明。价位约束改变价格与优先激励。',
    "ETF arbitrage depends on executable baskets, settlement and capital; the March twenty-twenty case is sourced literature. The initial March facility covered investment-grade bond ETFs; high-yield eligibility expanded in April. A unique role-indifference spread follows from the simplified equal-speed assumptions. Industry profit and pure-sniper transfers differ. A separate fixed-prize investment game can have a prisoner's dilemma. Rule thirty-eight is a proposed validation standard.": 'ETF套利依赖可执行篮子、结算和资本，2020年3月案例来自文献。3月最初设施覆盖投资级债券ETF，4月扩展高收益资格。简化等速假设导出唯一角色无差异价差；行业利润不同于纯狙击者转移。独立固定奖池投资博弈可以有囚徒困境。第38条是拟议验证标准。',
    "Three lessons. <bookmark mark='a'/> Gross execution revenue and horizon-consistent marked gains need one consistent ledger. <bookmark mark='b'/> Reach probabilities, quote-control models and executable profit are different objects requiring different validation. <bookmark mark='c'/> Tick, priority and batch rules change incentives, but a welfare conclusion needs explicit resource costs, information and participation assumptions.": "三个教训。<bookmark mark='a'/>毛执行收入与一致时限标记收益需要同一个相容账本。<bookmark mark='b'/>触达概率、报价控制模型和可执行利润是不同对象，需要不同验证。<bookmark mark='c'/>价位、优先和批量规则改变激励，但福利结论需要明确资源、信息与参与假设。",
    'The formulas with their scopes. Horizon edge uses execution edge and adverse markout once. The exponential rate is a model, fed here with reach proxies. GLFT is an interior approximation, with finite-inventory qualifications. The ETF band uses executable basket values. The sniping root is conditional on equal-speed role assumptions. The batch expression is a separate uniform-phase, fixed-latency exposure heuristic, not the output of the batch-flag simulation.': '公式及其范围。时限边际只使用一次执行边际和不利标记。指数到达率是模型，此处输入触达代理。GLFT为带有限库存限定的内点近似。ETF区间用可执行篮子值。狙击根依赖等速角色假设。批量公式是另一个统一相位、固定延迟暴露启发式，不是批量标志模拟的输出。',
    "How this part connects. <bookmark mark='a'/> Backwards: Part thirty-five's dealer models become a business with costs; Part thirty-six's markouts become its profit and loss; Part thirty-seven's executor is its customer. <bookmark mark='b'/> Sideways: Part eleven's options maker is the same business in another product. <bookmark mark='c'/> Forwards: Part thirty-nine's automated makers quote by formula, Part forty-one's crises are when makers step back, and Part forty-two's learning agents take the maker's chair.": "这一部分如何与其他部分相连。<bookmark mark='a'/>往回看：第35部分的交易商模型变成了有成本的生意；第36部分的事后损益变成了它的损益；第37部分的执行者是它的客户。<bookmark mark='b'/>横向看：第11部分的期权做市商是另一种产品中的同一门生意。<bookmark mark='c'/>往前看：第39部分的自动做市商按公式报价，第41部分的危机是做市商退出的时候，第42部分的学习型主体坐上做市商的椅子。",
    "Six desk questions. How should a maker account for profit? Keep a consistent marked-wealth ledger, and do not subtract a horizon mark twice. <bookmark mark='a'/> Why skew inventory? To change the arrival incentives within the chosen model. <bookmark mark='b'/> What do reach probabilities establish? Threshold frequencies, not actual queue fills or a validated optimal quote.": "六个桌面问题。利润如何核算？保持一致的标记财富账本，不重复扣时限标记。<bookmark mark='a'/>为何倾斜库存？在选定模型内改变到达激励。<bookmark mark='b'/>触达概率建立什么？阈值频率，不是实际队列成交或已验证最优报价。",
    "What does a pinned spread change? It can shift competition toward priority, while actual rents need further evidence. <bookmark mark='a'/> What keeps an ETF near basket value? Executable creation and redemption, subject to costs and constraints rather than a hard bound at a stale published NAV. <bookmark mark='b'/> What does the sniping root establish? A conditional role spread. Industry revenue, pure-sniper transfers and investment welfare are different quantities. Complete answers are in the notes.": "被价位约束的价差改变什么？它可使竞争转向优先，实际租金仍需额外证据。<bookmark mark='a'/>什么让ETF靠近篮子值？受成本与约束的可执行申赎，而非陈旧公布净值的硬界。<bookmark mark='b'/>狙击根建立什么？有条件的角色价差。行业收入、纯狙击者转移及投资福利是不同量，完整答案在笔记。",
    "The random-jump pause. <bookmark mark='a'/> With investor rate ten, jump rate two and magnitude three, the root is half a tick. <bookmark mark='b'/> A one-or-five mixture has the same root because both magnitudes exceed half a tick. The positive-part function is linear on that support. Convex-order increases can leave the root unchanged; a strict widening needs additional excess mass at the relevant kink, not a generic statement about tails.": "随机幅度暂停。<bookmark mark='a'/>投资者率十、跳跃率二、幅度三，根为半档。<bookmark mark='b'/>一或五的混合也给半档，因为两幅度都超过根，正部函数在该支持上线性。凸序增大可以不改变根；严格变宽需在相关折点处增加超额质量，不能泛称尾部必然如此。",
    "Twelve problems with complete bilingual solutions. Six basic problems cover consistent edge accounting, the Avellaneda and Stoikov approximation, Poisson-equivalent rate conversion, selected replay losses, a fixed-mid tick markup and executable ETF redemption. <bookmark mark='a'/> Four advanced problems distinguish random priority and industry accounting, the random-jump root, batch exposure from a spread ratio, and strict dominance in an explicitly specified four-firm investment game. <bookmark mark='b'/> The two qualifying problems prove the integrable random-magnitude root and convex-order comparison, then derive the CARA HJB, quote first-order condition, finite-inventory linear system and spectral limit. The exact fixed-cap risk-neutral limit must be distinguished from the interior Gaussian approximation. All units and additional assumptions belong to the problems, not to claims of identified market profit.": "十二题均有完整双语解答。六道基础题包括一致边际、阿韦利亚内达与斯托伊科夫近似、泊松等效转换、选定回放损失、固定中点价位加成及可执行ETF赎回。<bookmark mark='a'/>四道进阶题区分随机优先与行业核算、随机跳幅根、批量暴露与价差比，以及明确四家投资博弈中的严格占优。<bookmark mark='b'/>两道资格题证明可积幅度的根与凸序比较，再推导恒定绝对风险厌恶HJB、报价一阶条件、有限库存线性系统及谱极限。固定上限的精确风险中性极限必须区别于高斯内点近似。题目的单位与额外假设不是已识别市场利润的声明。",
    "Where this comes back. Part thirty-nine replaces quotes with a pricing curve: the automated market maker. Part forty-one asks who provides liquidity when it vanishes. Part forty-two puts learning agents in the maker's chair. And Part forty-three asks whether anyone beats the market after paying the makers.": '这些内容会在哪里再出现。第39部分用一条定价曲线取代报价：自动做市商。第41部分问流动性消失时由谁提供。第42部分让学习型主体坐上做市商的椅子。第43部分问，在付钱给做市商之后，是否有人能战胜市场。',
    'The cited textbooks and papers distinguish models from attributed institutional evidence. Our successful numerical originals use public Binance inputs and stipulated simulations. Chosen arithmetic is labeled separately. The ETF discussion uses the cited BIS study and official term sheets, with no newly verified price series. Exact audits, the rejected input and final review limitations are retained in the notes.': '所引教材和论文区分模型与署名制度证据。成功数值原函数使用币安公开输入与规定模拟；指定算术另标。ETF讨论使用所引国际清算银行研究与官方条款，没有新验证价格序列。精确审计、拒绝输入和最终审阅局限均在笔记保留。',
    "The House has a proposed framework for measuring quoting costs and testing model assumptions, not a completed live market-making business. <bookmark mark='a'/> Next, Part thirty-nine: crypto and decentralized finance, perpetual funding, curve-based liquidity and venue failures. The same distinctions between accounting, assumptions and identified evidence will matter there.": "量化之家有测量报价成本和检验模型假设的拟议框架，不是已经完成的实盘做市业务。<bookmark mark='a'/>下一部分第39部分：加密与去中心化金融、永续资金费、曲线流动性及场所失败。核算、假设和识别证据的区别在那里同样重要。",
}
